{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style","id":1478958,"title":"[Deviant] Ask a Simple Question, Renegade-Style","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Deviant: The Renegades"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-16T09:21:21-07:00","id":1478958,"title":"[Deviant] Ask a Simple Question, Renegade-Style","content":"Since the game's been out long enough and no special forum is likely forthcoming, I thought there should be a thread for people to bandy about some Deviant discourse.<br /> <br /> I'll start with a question of my own: How do Variation effects that are limited to once per chapter/scene interact with Involuntary Scars? Can the Storyteller force the character to activate an Adaptation like Iron Will if the Scar would oblige the use of an effect that hasn't reset yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-16T13:49:13-07:00","id":1478973,"title":"","content":"Off the top of my head, I would not have an Involuntary Scar trigger the use of a Variation that's on cooldown. Its disadvantage is that it can &quot;waste&quot; the Variation by triggering it when you don't need it, leaving it stuck in cooldown when you actually do need it. This is without refernecing the book text right now, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-16T17:33:58-07:00","id":1478988,"title":"","content":"Running down the list of core Variation effects for which this is relevant:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">\u2022 Environmental Adaptation (General Deviation only)<br /> \u2022 Face Thief 4 (Social Merit effect only, per-target)<br /> \u2022 Gigantic (post-use healing only)<br /> \u2022 Healer 4 (general limitation is per-effect-per-target and thus applies as much from deliberate use as involuntary)<br /> \u2022 Shadows of the Past 3+ (Living History; general limitation is per-target and thus applies as much from deliberate use as involuntary)<br /> \u2022 Storm-Caller (Universal Deviation only)<br /> \u2022 Astral Travel 4+ (Dream Walker)<br /> \u2022 Animal Transformation (Shapeshifter Deviation only)<br /> \u2022 Blessing (all effects)<br /> \u2022 Fate's Agent (Universal Deviation only)<br /> \u2022 Precognition 3 and 4 (Bifurcation effect)<br /> \u2022 Computer-Aided Programming (all effects)<br /> \u2022 Hidden Compartments (potentially all effects with Varied Inventory Deviation)<br /> \u2022 Omnicompetence 2+ (all effects)<br /> \u2022 Sensory Array (all effects)<br /> \u2022 Inhuman Digestion 3 (Variation removal only)<br /> \u2022 Sacred Flesh (Secretion and Fragment methods only)</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'd disagree that the disadvantage of Involuntary Scars is that they can &quot;waste&quot; the Variation \u2014 the key disadvantage both core Involuntary Scars impose beyond their lowest Magnitude is that they and all their entangled Variations become Overt if they trigger, which draws conspiracy attention more easily.<br /> <br /> Relatedly, the fact that both core Involuntary Scars' mechanically-backed manifestations allow a Scar Resistance roll to prevent them means that, yes, I would have Involuntary Scars apply the cost of the deviant's repeater Adaptation if it would be required to use the Variation again within that window; much as Involuntary activation doesn't allow a deviant to get around needing an instant action to steer Directed Variations, it likewise shouldn't allow them to get around the limitations of how often they can safely use the power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-21T12:37:04-07:00","id":1479257,"title":"","content":"Interesting stuff to think about both ways. I suppose consistency within a given game is key, regardless.<br /> <br /> Actually speaking of Adaptations, does Untameable work on Standard Deviations attached to a Scar? As strictly interpreted, I think the answer is yes, since the effect treats the Scar as Magnitude 1 for the rest of the scene, but there are a number of SDs that alter the fundamentals of how entangled Variations work that might run counter to character concept (you can normally only use Electrokinesis on targets you physically touch, which you've already described as being the result of possessing implanted knifefish organs, but occasionally suddenly you can wield the power at range).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-21T17:31:59-07:00","id":1479267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1479257#post1479257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting stuff to think about both ways. I suppose consistency within a given game is key, regardless.<br /> <br /> Actually speaking of Adaptations, does Untameable work on Standard Deviations attached to a Scar? As strictly interpreted, I think the answer is yes, since the effect treats the Scar as Magnitude 1 for the rest of the scene, but there are a number of SDs that alter the fundamentals of how entangled Variations work that might run counter to character concept (you can normally only use Electrokinesis on targets you physically touch, which you've already described as being the result of possessing implanted knifefish organs, but occasionally suddenly you can wield the power at range).</div> </div> </div> </div>Answer is yes. All the &quot;this only works through touch&quot; examples are Power Failure-based, for which the mechanical handling of Mag 1 is as described.<br /> <br /> As for running counter to character concept, there's the twofold answer of &quot;then don't do that&quot; and &quot;deviant powers come from having their souls cracked open and so things occasionally getting weird is par for the course.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Possibly not a simple question, but: given the &quot;no secondary Scars that apply secondary Scars&quot; restriction, how can one model a Cyborg who can turn off their sense-enhancing Variations at the cost of their senses if Suppressible Variation &gt; Persistent Drawback &gt; Sensory Deprivation is not a mechanically valid approach?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-22T05:01:40-07:00","id":1479290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1479267#post1479267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possibly not a simple question, but: given the &quot;no secondary Scars that apply secondary Scars&quot; restriction, how can one model a Cyborg who can turn off their sense-enhancing Variations at the cost of their senses if Suppressible Variation &gt; Persistent Drawback &gt; Sensory Deprivation is not a mechanically valid approach?</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds like a place to ignore the letter of the law to carry out the spirit of the law. The &quot;no secondary Scars that apply secondary Scars&quot; restriction is meant to cut down on cheese and keep things simple, but since the outcome you are going for is both simple to understand and not cheese I think most STs would permit it. In the case that your ST wouldn't allow it, though, you could probably use Mimicry with Sensory Deprivation, though that's less elegant than your initial idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-22T07:32:22-07:00","id":1479298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1479267#post1479267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possibly not a simple question, but: given the &amp;quot;no secondary Scars that apply secondary Scars&amp;quot; restriction, how can one model a Cyborg who can turn off their sense-enhancing Variations at the cost of their senses if Suppressible Variation &gt; Persistent Drawback &gt; Sensory Deprivation is not a mechanically valid approach?</div> </div> </div> </div>Another approach would be to add the Mimicry Variation, with Persistent Drawback (Sensory Deprivation) as the Scar. Though this would mean the cyborg could potentially suppress other Variations/Scars all by turning off their senses. Which could get a little strange to try and justify, especially since you can pick and choose which Variations to suppress each time you activate Mimicry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-22T08:52:42-07:00","id":1479302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1479298#post1479298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Another approach would be to add the Mimicry Variation, with Persistent Drawback (Sensory Deprivation) as the Scar. Though this would mean the cyborg could potentially suppress other Variations/Scars all by turning off their senses. Which could get a little strange to try and justify, especially since you can pick and choose which Variations to suppress each time you activate Mimicry.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> you could just limit yourself voluntarily (OOC) to always suppress the same set of Variations each time","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-30T14:39:18-07:00","id":1479838,"title":"","content":"Does having Face Thief active override the effects of Conspicuous Appearance, or does this result in the borrowed appearance having a &quot;tell&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-30T16:10:20-07:00","id":1479842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1479838#post1479838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does having Face Thief active override the effects of Conspicuous Appearance, or does this result in the borrowed appearance having a &quot;tell&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd err against having a Variation directly counteract a Scar. Though, as a Storyteller, I'd avoid having the Conspicuous aspect cause the Face Thief disguise fail outright. Though that becomes a stretch at the higher Magnitudes of Conspicuous Appearance.<br /> <br /> And/or if Face Thief is entangled with a scar other than Conspicuous Appearance, then you could combine Face Thief with Mimicry in a Monstrous Transformation, or give Conspicuous Appearance the Suppressible Variation: Power Failure (Face Thief Active) deviation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":23730,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","user":"Scriptorian","date":". 04-30-2022, 07:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T18:50:35-07:00","id":1480232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1479842#post1479842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd err against having a Variation directly counteract a Scar. Though, as a Storyteller, I'd avoid having the Conspicuous aspect cause the Face Thief disguise fail outright. Though that becomes a stretch at the higher Magnitudes of Conspicuous Appearance.</div> </div> </div> </div>My impulses are that\u2026<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>As an Overt Variation with an ongoing Willpower cost to manage from scene to scene, it doesn't really break much to trade a specific form of attention-getting for a draining but less extreme form of attention-getting, but\u2026</li> <li>&quot;Thing that looks like someone you know but with an incongruous detail that gives it away&quot; is a classic shapeshifter trope for a reason, Conspicuous Appearance 3- allows for the tell to be concealable to varying degrees, the Scar specifically mentions as examples things that shapeshifting wouldn't help with (e.g. uncanny mannerisms, unsettling grace, constant minor levitation, trails of fire), the Scar can be Physical or Social, and the Variation isn't a full-body perfect disguise until Magnitude 3 (which leaves gaps for the Scar's giveaways to poke through) but <i>does</i> give the rote quality to Subterfuge rolls to successfully apply a disguise (and the rolls to conceal your Conspicuous Appearance are listed as Wits + Subterfuge in the Magnitude 2 version and immediately described as rolls to disguise or hide the character's appearance in the Magnitude 3 version). Also\u2026</li> <li>It would be kind of hypocritical of me to suppose that Face Thief can override blatant inhumanity when I've elsewhere voiced the opinion that it's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1478471-deviants-variation-build-advice?p=1478495#post1478495\">not the solution to Relentless Animal Transformation</a>.</li> </ol><br /> Different question: Does Tribulation 4's wording mean that the Variation roll succeeding takes one instant action, and then on a successful roll, you have to spend the Willpower on a second instant action before the Variation activates according to the resolution determined by the roll in the previous turn? Because if not then I'm not sure how to square it with the stipulations for Controlled Scar costs on page 107, of which Tribulation is a specific example. The fact that the Magnitude math makes the four-dot version mutually incompatible with the Deviation that can only apply to Directed Variations feels like an easy out to the complications of &quot;when does the target roll to resist?&quot; and &quot;what if you target somebody who moves out of range in the turn between rolling and spending Willpower?&quot;<br /> <br /> Anyone have thoughts on this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T21:46:17-07:00","id":1480261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1480232#post1480232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My impulses are that\u2026 [LIST=1]<br /> Different question: Does Tribulation 4's wording mean that the Variation roll succeeding takes one instant action, and then on a successful roll, you have to spend the Willpower on a second instant action before the Variation activates according to the resolution determined by the roll in the previous turn? Because if not then I'm not sure how to square it with the stipulations for Controlled Scar costs on page 107, of which Tribulation is a specific example. The fact that the Magnitude math makes the four-dot version mutually incompatible with the Deviation that can only apply to Directed Variations feels like an easy out to the complications of &quot;when does the target roll to resist?&quot; and &quot;what if you target somebody who moves out of range in the turn between rolling and spending Willpower?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Two actions, yes, one to roll to activate the Variation according to normal Controlled rules, the results of which &quot;hang&quot; for a turn, and then if you succeeded, the next turn you spend the Willpower and actually get to roll out the &quot;hanging&quot; activation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-09T10:31:34-07:00","id":1480558,"title":"","content":"With Immunity 1, a character can resist the Poisoned Tilt, but it's not until Immunity 2 that a Deviant may gain full protection against poisons; what are some good in-setting justifications for this, and what is the best way to portray the distinction when it matters (besides more in-depth poison rules)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-09T17:53:18-07:00","id":1480604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1480558#post1480558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Immunity 1, a character can resist the Poisoned Tilt, but it's not until Immunity 2 that a Deviant may gain full protection against poisons; what are some good in-setting justifications for this, and what is the best way to portray the distinction when it matters (besides more in-depth poison rules)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Action scenes represent a higher-energy state of affairs that the body can more easily be primed to safeguard against; it's like how you can lose an arm and survive but die of blood loss from a bunch of smaller cuts. Same goes for the Sick Tilt versus Disease \u2014 being in a fistfight or a car chase with Immunity 1 will allow you to function normally, but you'll still be fighting off malaria in the long term.<br /> <br /> Less in-setting, Immunity is a non-scalable Discrete Variation whose Magnitude 1 and 2 versions provide multiple immunities unless you're working with Scar Power 1 \u2014 it's on both lists so you don't have to take multiple Variations to be immune to both Cold and Disease or Poisoned and Arm Wrack.<br /> <br /> It's certainly not a matter of cost alone \u2014 Anomalous Biology (Heartless) provides immunity to both poison and disease at the debatable price of a Subtle giveaway that you're not a Baseline, and Healer 2 or 3 and Rapid Healing 3 functionally negate poison and disease from the same angle \u2014 but if you're got Immunity to Poison or the Poisoned Tilt, that's because of an expressed Variation of Immunity rather than not having a heartbeat or being able to undo the damage as it comes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-09T18:01:51-07:00","id":1480607,"title":"","content":"One-dot immunity to the Poisoned Tilt can be flavored as your system being hardy enough to fight off fast-acting poisons during adrenaline-charged action scenes. It doesn't immunize against Toxicity (p. 206) or related Conditions such as Intoxicated. So kind of a poison-resistance equivalent to the difference between a marathon runner and a sprinter, where you can manage bursts of fast metabolism but still suffer longer-term debilitation. Probably not scientific, but a lot of the Remade defy conventional biophysics anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T20:57:56-07:00","id":1481815,"title":"","content":"Does Deadly Ichor share Lash's ability to be purchased any number of times to represent different modes of counterattack?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T04:25:31-07:00","id":1481986,"title":"","content":"Why not? The rulebook already allow you to purchase some variations more than once, after all.<br /> <br /> I have a question as well, the player can purchase variations from not native clades? Like a cephalist having chimerical variations and so on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2457,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","user":"Ipergigio","date":". 05-26-2022, 07:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T05:02:10-07:00","id":1481987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1481986#post1481986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question as well, the player can purchase variations from not native clades? Like a cephalist having chimerical variations and so on?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. See the Characters Creation's &quot;Variations&quot; heading (p77), and &quot;Acquiring Variations&quot; (p108).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T10:34:27-07:00","id":1482006,"title":"","content":"Generally, no. Deadly Ichor already strains action economy. Allowing it to counterattack multiple times for every successful incoming attack would be a huge headache. That being said, if you limit it to one counter per attacker per turn (as is already stated in the RAW) regardless of how many Deadly Ichor versions you have, you could probably allow it at a table without such nightmarish consequences. Explaining it in-world might be a bit more complicated, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T15:26:19-07:00","id":1482199,"title":"","content":"Hello it's me once again!<br /> <br /> According to rules, you have to pay a &quot;conspiracy point&quot; to buy a Variation Deviation. But what about Scar Deviations? You have to pay for them as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T16:29:42-07:00","id":1482202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1482199#post1482199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to rules, you have to pay a &quot;conspiracy point&quot; to buy a Variation Deviation. But what about Scar Deviations? You have to pay for them as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea what you mean by this.<br /> <br /> Deviations are gained by increasing the the Magnitude of their Variation or Scar as a floating alternative to going up to the next level of their default ladder of effects. You increase Variation Magnitude by having the entangled Scar Magnitude go up enough to support the change. Scar Magnitude goes up by marking medium or major Instability in your last five Stability boxes.<br /> <br /> Conspiracies have no direct mechanical impact on gaining Deviations \u2014 the reverse can be said, given how Standing is calculated as part of Threat Level at the beginning of a chronicle or for an unconnected conspiracy taking the main antagonist slot after the old one is destroyed, but none of the mechanics that could be described as &quot;conspiracy points&quot; have anything to do with rules for how a Deviant develops their powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T22:52:12-07:00","id":1482219,"title":"","content":"But the dot you can put on your variations aren't determined by the conspiracy level threat plus a free scar dot?<br /> And variation/scar deviations have a cost as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2457,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","user":"Ipergigio","date":". 05-29-2022, 01:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T01:17:04-07:00","id":1482228,"title":"","content":"Your character starts play with a total Magnitude of Variations as specified by Threat Level, plus your Origin's Scar-free dot.<br /> <br /> Every Variation must be entangled with one Scar of equal or greater Magnitude, ignoring that one Scar-free dot. Scars may entangle multiple Variations of lesser Magnitude, but Variations never entangle with multiple Scars, no matter the Magnitude.<br /> <br /> Deviations modify the effective Magnitude of their corresponding Variation or Scar. So a Magnitude 2 Variation with a +1 Deviation, a Magnitude 3 Variation with no Deviations, and a Magnitude 4 Deviation with a -1 Deviation all have the same effective Magnitude of 3 and must be entangled with at least a Magnitude 3 Scar. (Unless, of course, one of those dots of Variation Magnitude is the Scar-free dot, in which case you need at least a Magnitude 2 Scar.)<br /> <br /> Scar Variations modify the effective Magnitude of their corresponding Scar the same way. A Magnitude 2 Scar with a +1 Deviation, a Magnitude 3 Scar with no Deviations, and a Magnitude 4 Scar with a -1 Deviation all have the same effective Magnitude of 3, and can thus entangle either one Magnitude 3 Variation, two Magnitude 2 Variations, or three Magnitude 1 Variations.<br /> <br /> Deviations with positive values, like +1, exaggerate the trait they modify. Positive Variation Deviations make the Variation more powerful in some way. Positive Scar Deviations make the Scar more debilitating. Conversely, negative Deviations make Variations weaker or Scars less severe.<br /> <br /> For the most part nothing cares whether a dot of Magnitude is being allocated to the base Variation/Scar or to a positive Deviation layered on top. It's all just entangling Variations to Scars and making sure the Scar Magnitude can support the Variations the Scar entangles. Do remember, though, that the Deviation's effects are layered on top of the effects of the pre-modified Variation or Scar. If a Variation deals bashing damage when bought at Magnitude 2 or lethal at Magnitude 3, and you buy it at Magnitude 2 and raise its Magnitude by adding a +1 Deviation that lets the Variation deal Leg Wrack or something, it's still going to do bashing damage and not lethal, even though you've raised its effective final Magnitude to 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 05-29-2022, 04:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T04:04:07-07:00","id":1482237,"title":"","content":"And how many deviations can you apply to variations and scars?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T04:52:21-07:00","id":1482241,"title":"","content":"The effective Magnitude of a Variation or Scar after applying Deviations can't exceed 5. That's the only restriction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T06:34:55-07:00","id":1482246,"title":"","content":"This character creation is going to harm my mental healt! Deviant isn't user friendly at all!<br /> <br /> I'm about to play a level 7 threat story.<br /> I have 7 + 1 dots for my variations, if I apply a +1 deviation to a magnitude 2 variation, it will cost me 3 dots at character creation, I'm right?<br /> <br /> About scars deviations are free, the only limit is to not go below 1 and above 5 on magnitude?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T07:19:11-07:00","id":1482249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1482246#post1482246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This character creation is going to harm my mental healt! Deviant isn't user friendly at all!<br /> <br /> I'm about to play a level 7 threat story.<br /> I have 7 + 1 dots for my variations, if I apply a +1 deviation to a magnitude 2 variation, it will cost me 3 dots at character creation, I'm right?<br /> <br /> About scars deviations are free, the only limit is to not go below 1 and above 5 on magnitude?</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay.<br /> <br /> Threat Level is a six-level scale that determines the Standing of the chronicle's initial antagonist conspiracy directly (the first Threat Level starts with a Standing 1 conspiracy, the second Threat Level starts with a Standing 2 conspiracy, etc) and the total Magnitude of Variations a character starts with that must be accounted for by the Magnitude of their Scars (approximately Threat Level*2.5, round down).<br /> <br /> Deviations modify the Magnitude of the Scar or Variation they are attached to by the amount listed on the Deviation. The only Deviations that &quot;don't count&quot; are ones that add or subtract 0 Magnitude. You have to have enough Scar Magnitude to support the Magnitudes of the Variations you start with, whether by entangling each Variation with a Scar of equal Magnitude or entangling a single Scar with multiple lower-Magnitude Variations. A Scar can support one Variation of equal Magnitude, two Variations of a Magnitude one less than its own, three Variations of a Magnitude two less than its own, etc. Magnitude cannot go above 5 or below 1 on Scars or Variations.<br /> <br /> If you are playing a chronicle whose starting Threat Level is Dysplasia, you have a Standing 3 conspiracy after you and 7 Magnitude of Variations that need to be accounted for with Scar Magnitude.<br /> <br /> That Variation Magnitude could be accounted for through the Magnitude of the Variations' default effects entirely, or you could apply Deviations to raise the Magnitude without getting a higher-level basic effect \u2014 for example, you could have Bioluminescence 3 and either be able to project a beam of light bright enough to completely blind someone if Directed into their eyes (the normal Magnitude 3 effect), or you could make your whole body glow brightly enough to partially blind everyone within 40 yards with the Aura Deviation (+1 Magnitude on the Magnitude 2 effect).<br /> <br /> The Scar Magnitude, again, just needs to be sufficient to support the Variations you have. If you have Brachiation 2, Carapace 3, Lash 2, you could entangle those respectively with Addictive Variation 2, Phobia 3, and Bestial Mind 2 (and the 3 dots of Magnitude in Phobia can come from having a phobia that you can't spend Willpower to overcome, a Common phobia that you <i>can</i> spend Willpower to overcome, or a Rare phobia that makes you Frightened or Insensate)<br /> <br /> Alternately, you could entangle the two Magnitude 2 Variations (Brachiation and Carapace) with Conspicuous Appearance 3, giving you a smaller number of Scars to deal with at the cost of those Scars being worse without giving you access to a more powerful Variation; by the same token, you could entangle all three Variations with Phobia 5, which works the same as it would for Carapace 3 alone, except you would need to apply a Standard Deviation like Identifier, Nightmares, or Disfiguring Scar to increase the Magnitude of a Phobia that doesn't have the Common Deviation to bring its Magnitude up to 5, since Phobia does not have a Magnitude 5 effect in its default string of effects and it doesn't have any other +1 Deviations besides Common (which cannot be combined with Rare).<br /> <br /> The Scar-free dot effectively allows you to treat the Variation it's applied to as though it were one dot lower for the purposes of Scar entanglement, such that, in the example above, you could increase the Magnitude of Brachiation, Carapace, or Lash by 1 (which one depends on the character's Origin) and not need to increase the Magnitude of any of the Scars to support it.<br /> <br /> In sum: A Magnitude 3 Variation needs to be entangled with a Scar of at least Magnitude 3. Magnitude goes from 1 to 5, no lower or higher; within those limits, Deviations increase the Magnitude of their Variation or Scar by the amount listed on the Deviation. The only &quot;free&quot; thing in the process is the dot of subtle or overt Variation Magnitude afforded to you by your Origin. Total Magnitude by Threat Level is portioned across your starting Variations, which then need Scar Magnitude that can support those Variations individually and/or in combination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Corrected the example of entangling multiple Variations with a single Scar. 05-29-2022, 10:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T07:52:22-07:00","id":1482251,"title":"","content":"Ok I guess I'm starting to understand this is my wish list for my 7 magnitude dots:<br /> <br /> VARIATIONS:<br /> 1 dot Lash <br /> 1 dot Lash<br /> 2 dot Otherwordly Connection (clade's free dot)<br /> 4 dot Monstrous Tranformation<br /> <br /> SCARS:<br /> 2 dot Cooldown<br /> 2 dot Bane<br /> 4 dot Alternate Persona (deviations: invocation, superior persona)<br /> <br /> Is anything correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T08:51:57-07:00","id":1482253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1482251#post1482251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok I guess I'm starting to understand this is my wish list for my 7 magnitude dots:<br /> <br /> VARIATIONS:<br /> 1 dot Lash<br /> 1 dot Lash<br /> 2 dot Otherwordly Connection (clade's free dot)<br /> 4 dot Monstrous Tranformation<br /> <br /> SCARS:<br /> 2 dot Cooldown<br /> 2 dot Bane<br /> 4 dot Alternate Persona (deviations: invocation, superior persona)<br /> <br /> Is anything correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Otherworldly Connection 2 with the free dot counts as a Magnitude 1 Variation for the purposes of Scar entanglement, so you could either reduce the Magnitude of whichever Scar it's entangled with by 1 or get rid of one of the Magnitude 2 Scars and increase the Magnitude of the other to 3 and still have a valid setup. (You can also keep the excess Scar Magnitude, which can be used to entangle new Variations when you have the 4 Experiences to buy a new Variation.)<br /> <br /> Also, your Scar-free dot of Variation Magnitude does not have anything to do with your Clade. Your Scar-free dot of Variation Magnitude comes from your Origin. Your Clade's mechanical impact on your Variations is that you can't have more than half of your total Variation Magnitude come from Clade Variations other than your own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T14:07:14-07:00","id":1482287,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much! Finally I got it... hopefully.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T09:42:27-07:00","id":1482378,"title":"","content":"Hopefully the final question.<br /> <br /> My idea is about a human permanently fettered by a spirit. Which form adapt better to my concept?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T10:05:31-07:00","id":1482381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1482378#post1482378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My idea is about a human permanently fettered by a spirit. Which form adapt better to my concept?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's got any influence over the character's Variations, Symbiote; anything else is going to depend on other details.<br /> <br /> Worth noting that simply being Fettered to a person can last indefinitely and doesn't usually break open their soul. What's the rest of the character concept?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T10:15:50-07:00","id":1482383,"title":"","content":"The spirit is fettered to the human and lurks around into the twilight, and if needed the spirit take control over the human triggering the Monstrous Transformation. This unisual fetteted condition may fuels the deviant variations and scars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2457,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","user":"Ipergigio","date":". 05-30-2022, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T14:42:28-07:00","id":1482407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1482383#post1482383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spirit is fettered to the human and lurks around into the twilight, and if needed the spirit take control over the human triggering the Monstrous Transformation. This unisual fetteted condition may fuels the deviant variations and scars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think what Satchel meant is, what makes this particular Fettered spirit so different from others? Why does being Urged literally break the character's soul and turn them into a fullblown Deviant in this particular case?<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, what happens if someone or something messes up the spirit that's just freely floating in Twilight?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 05-30-2022, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T16:32:42-07:00","id":1482418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1482407#post1482407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think what Satchel meant is, what makes this particular Fettered spirit so different from others? Why does being Urged literally break the character's soul and turn them into a fullblown Deviant in this particular case?<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, what happens if someone or something messes up the spirit that's just freely floating in Twilight?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this. A Coactive Divergence is more than just linking a spirit to an individual with the lightest possible touch \u2014 deviants of this sort are <i>infused</i>, which tends to mean the ephemeral being in question is either more thoroughly integrated or less specifically essential.<br /> <br /> Relatedly, why is Monstrous Transformation keyed to an Alternate Persona instead of an Involuntary Stimulus, particularly given (now that I look at it again) the Persona doesn't actually have enough positive Deviations for it be at Magnitude 4 from the base effect? Indelible Mark and the Unpredictable Deviation will go a long way if you're intending to model it as &quot;the spirit possesses the character whether they ask for it or not.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T04:06:35-07:00","id":1482471,"title":"","content":"Well, actually I'm triyng to emulate a sin-eater bound, but seems like it's going to be a pretty sophisticated task.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T04:38:23-07:00","id":1482476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1482471#post1482471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, actually I'm triyng to emulate a sin-eater bound, but seems like it's going to be a pretty sophisticated task.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case, why not just go with the Symbiote Form? You really don't need to stat out the spirit to have it hang around in Twilight. A Bound's Geist only has a projection in Twilight and can't act independently at all, unless it's Unleashed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T13:07:26-07:00","id":1482535,"title":"","content":"Should the modifications to the Deviant\u2019s bite attack made by Inhuman Digestion stack with any benefits they get to bitting from an Animal Transformation? What about with the Biting Swarm or Lethal Swarm transformations?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T13:52:02-07:00","id":1482540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1482535#post1482535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should the modifications to the Deviant\u2019s bite attack made by Inhuman Digestion stack with any benefits they get to bitting from an Animal Transformation? What about with the Biting Swarm or Lethal Swarm transformations?</div> </div> </div> </div>My instinct is to use the better rating from the two bite attacks, plus any extra bonus effects from either Variation, rather than direct stacking, though I couldn't say with certainty if that is what the authors intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-26T14:14:48-07:00","id":1485051,"title":"","content":"If a Deviant teleports beyond 1 yard while using the Camouflage Variation without the Mobile effect, does she still benefit from Camouflage or not?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-26T16:56:13-07:00","id":1485064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1485051#post1485051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Deviant teleports beyond 1 yard while using the Camouflage Variation without the Mobile effect, does she still benefit from Camouflage or not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that non-Mobile Camouflage frames the visual effects as &quot;blending into the background&quot; and says &quot;moves more than 1 yard/meter&quot; rather than &quot;moves more than 1 yard/meter per turn,&quot; my reading of the spirit of the effect is &quot;without the Mobile effect, Camouflage blends you in with the background of where you spent an instant action to toggle it, give or take a step in any direction.&quot; Teleportation will necessarily mess with that, as could be expected from using a Variation at Magnitude below 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-04T14:56:15-07:00","id":1485800,"title":"","content":"Is the Conspiracy Surveillance roll done for the whole cohort or each player separately?<br /> If a single roll is made for the whole cohort, how are the modifiers from different characters put together? E.g. one character lives of-the grid (-3), another instead has a bank account (+2)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-04T17:18:52-07:00","id":1485811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwhisper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1485800#post1485800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the Conspiracy Surveillance roll done for the whole cohort or each player separately?</div> </div> </div> </div>The former. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a single roll is made for the whole cohort, how are the modifiers from different characters put together? E.g. one character lives of-the grid (-3), another instead has a bank account (+2) </div> </div> </div>As long as the total modifiers don't exceed +/-5, it just goes as normal. Maybe the Storyteller angles the result toward the character contributing more bonuses; acting against known accomplices and allies of the cohort is substantially easier when those allies are responsible for their connections to modern society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-06T11:40:44-07:00","id":1485921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1485811#post1485811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The former.<br /> As long as the total modifiers don't exceed +/-5, it just goes as normal. Maybe the Storyteller angles the result toward the character contributing more bonuses; acting against known accomplices and allies of the cohort is substantially easier when those allies are responsible for their connections to modern society.</div> </div> </div> </div>So in a group of 4 players, what would the total modifier be if 3 were homeless (-2) and one rented an apartment (+2) ?<br /> What if instead 3 rented an apartment and one was homeless?<br /> <br /> If I understand correctly, there wouldn't be any difference between the two cases as they would both result in 0, right?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-06T14:49:27-07:00","id":1485942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwhisper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1485921#post1485921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in a group of 4 players, what would the total modifier be if 3 were homeless (-2) and one rented an apartment (+2) ?<br /> What if instead 3 rented an apartment and one was homeless?<br /> <br /> If I understand correctly, there wouldn't be any difference between the two cases as they would both result in 0, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>If those are the only modifying factors, I think that would be a net -4 and a net +4, respectively, since there are three of one and one of the other, not an even split.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-07T04:40:52-07:00","id":1485976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1485942#post1485942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If those are the only modifying factors, I think that would be a net -4 and a net +4, respectively, since there are three of one and one of the other, not an even split.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with adding up penalties is that it scales up with the number of players. Which means that 4 homeless characters are harder to track than 2, and it doesn't make sense to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> It would make sense if the roll was to find *all the characters at once*, but the way I understand it the Surveillance roll represents the Conspiracy getting a blip on their radar, *any* blip.<br /> <br /> <br /> I just started running a chronicle with 5 players. It seems that if 3 or 4 of them satisfy some circumstances like homeless or unemployed, the penalty will still outweight even the use of magnitude 5 overt variations.<br /> <br /> <br /> It seems weird that having more characters chased by the same conspiracy increases Nodes and Attributes but not surveillance dice pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26440,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","user":"moonwhisper","date":". 07-07-2022, 08:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-07T16:07:33-07:00","id":1486012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwhisper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1485976#post1485976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems weird that having more characters chased by the same conspiracy increases Nodes and Attributes but not surveillance dice pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it seems weird to me to count a cohort as both &quot;homeless&quot; and &quot;owns a house&quot; considering how cohorts are described in the book, particularly given the splat's relation to the Safe Place Merit, but that was the premise of the question.<br /> <br /> The most sensible read is probably to use the modifier for living situation that most benefits the roll for the whole cohort, given the aforementioned &quot;angle the result toward the character contributing the most bonuses&quot; thing and treat the cohort as a collective character for which each modifier can apply once. The cohort isn't homeless if one of them owns a home unless for some reason the one who owns a home refuses to let the rest crash at their place or associate with them, at which point the question arises of how a cohort with Deviant Problems can cohere.<br /> <br /> It's definitely not the intention that each character has a separate Surveillance roll for them, because the conspiracy does not get a scaling number of Conspiracy Actions to act against the cohort with based on number of players, and the Surveillance roll still provides the opportunity for action even on a failure (and past a certain combination of Standing and highest Overt Scar/Variation it's impossible for it to do worse than fail thanks to the modifier cap in relation to the core dicepool).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T22:48:41-07:00","id":1489059,"title":"","content":"Since most other splats have their own spiritual realms including the Underworld, does Deviant have its own realms, or does it include everything from every other splats since the Remades can basically be anything?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25803-omichli","name":"Omichli","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T02:21:11-07:00","id":1489077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omichli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1489059#post1489059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since most other splats have their own spiritual realms including the Underworld, does Deviant have its own realms, or does it include everything from every other splats since the Remades can basically be anything?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes to the latter, though the underworld of society is divorced from most peoples\u2019 daily lives to count as an \u2018Otherworld\u2019 I think, and that\u2019s the main focus. Sorta like how Vampire (and Hunter) does it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T10:42:07-07:00","id":1489135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omichli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1489059#post1489059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since most other splats have their own spiritual realms including the Underworld, does Deviant have its own realms, or does it include everything from every other splats since the Remades can basically be anything?</div> </div> </div> </div>Deviants are tuned to expect most of their antagonists to be human conspirators, and so the corebook Variations don't really make them much better than ordinary humans at interdimensional travel. Remade with Coactive Variations can interact with ephemeral entities such as spirits and ghosts, but generally they interact with those that have already breached or been stranded in the material realm.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T17:31:05-07:00","id":1489171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omichli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1489059#post1489059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since most other splats have their own spiritual realms including the Underworld, does Deviant have its own realms, or does it include everything from every other splats since the Remades can basically be anything?</div> </div> </div> </div>As highlighted above, in practical terms, Deviants as a whole are in the same place as half of the other splats* as far as extradimensional travel goes: they inhabit the mortal material world of flesh and stone. They can hypothetically develop abilities relating to visitors and intrusive phenomena from outside the setting's primary stage, but the demands of Conviction and Loyalty tend to make messing around in other worlds a pursuit that will strain their connection to humanity outside of very particular circumstances. A character with high-Magnitude Conspicuous Appearance and/or whose Variations are in the End Stage might find themselves pulled into the deep end in that fashion, but the list of splats with easy access to the actual terrain of a different dimension are outliers compared to the rest of the world.<br /> <br /> * Vampire, Promethean, Hunter, Mummy, and Demon don't have another world they deal with mechanically by default in any sense more involved than awareness of a phase of Twilight; the Unchained have a tool for visiting the main otherworlds in a specific Exploit, and the Arisen can only get as far as the topmost layer of the Underworld via ghostly Twilight by chance; the closest thing Promethean has to a &quot;realm&quot; is the introduction of Azothic Memory in 2e, which isn't dealt with as a separate plane of existence, and Demon's closest equivalent to &quot;another world&quot; is explicitly God-Machine facilities being products of folded space and/or phased into Twilight; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1472918-vampire-otherworld?p=1472919#post1472919\">I've made the argument before</a> that Vampire notionally shares the same approximate &quot;otherworld&quot; as Deviant and Hunter, but that's very much more a thematic statement than a metaphysical one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T10:17:25-07:00","id":1489242,"title":"","content":"Vampire has Dis, the Lower Depth the Strix come from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T13:59:40-07:00","id":1489267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1489242#post1489242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire has Dis, the Lower Depth the Strix come from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dis is a black void only accessible with the help of the most powerful Strix, modern Strix are native to the mortal world, and nobody has anything they actually deal with there in a regular game. It has less impact on a game of Vampire than Duat does on a game of Mummy, never mind comparing it to the Shadow, the Underworld, the Hedge or the Astral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T14:15:48-07:00","id":1489269,"title":"","content":"True. Still, it\u2019s the closest thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T16:56:12-07:00","id":1489277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1489171#post1489171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As highlighted above, in practical terms, Deviants as a whole are in the same place as half of the other splats* as far as extradimensional travel goes: they inhabit the mortal material world of flesh and stone. They can hypothetically develop abilities relating to visitors and intrusive phenomena from outside the setting's primary stage, but the demands of Conviction and Loyalty tend to make messing around in other worlds a pursuit that will strain their connection to humanity outside of very particular circumstances. A character with high-Magnitude Conspicuous Appearance and/or whose Variations are in the End Stage might find themselves pulled into the deep end in that fashion, but the list of splats with easy access to the actual terrain of a different dimension are outliers compared to the rest of the world.<br /> <br /> * Vampire, Promethean, Hunter, Mummy, and Demon don't have another world they deal with mechanically by default in any sense more involved than awareness of a phase of Twilight; the Unchained have a tool for visiting the main otherworlds in a specific Exploit, and the Arisen can only get as far as the topmost layer of the Underworld via ghostly Twilight by chance; the closest thing Promethean has to a &quot;realm&quot; is the introduction of Azothic Memory in 2e, which isn't dealt with as a separate plane of existence, and Demon's closest equivalent to &quot;another world&quot; is explicitly God-Machine facilities being products of folded space and/or phased into Twilight; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1472918-vampire-otherworld?p=1472919#post1472919\">I've made the argument before</a> that Vampire notionally shares the same approximate &quot;otherworld&quot; as Deviant and Hunter, but that's very much more a thematic statement than a metaphysical one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see, thank you very much for the detailed explanation. I will have questions for the other splats soon.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25803-omichli","name":"Omichli","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T13:15:54-07:00","id":1489425,"title":"","content":"If someone has Monstrous Transformation 5, can they ever improve any of the entangled Variations under it? Regardless of which setup you chose (two 4's, three 3's, four 2's, etc), is there ever any way to raise them given Monstrous Transformation is already at 5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24242,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24242-honoraryorange","user":"honoraryorange","date":".  Typo fix 08-07-2022, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24242-honoraryorange","name":"honoraryorange","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T16:13:01-07:00","id":1489439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>honoraryorange</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1489425#post1489425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If someone has Monstrous Transformation 5, can they ever improve any of the entangled Variations under it? Regardless of which setup you chose (two 4's, three 3's, four 2's, etc), is there ever any way to raise them given Monstrous Transformation is already at 5?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not without still meeting the usual requirements for multiple Variations entangled with a single Scar, e.g. raising the Magnitude of a lower-level Variation to the current maximum or dropping an existing power from the list to bump everything else up. The primary benefit of Monstrous Transformation is the ability to activate multiple Variations in the same action, so effective forms tend to lean into the benefits of a lot of low-Magnitude Variations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T00:23:01-07:00","id":1490099,"title":"","content":"If I understand correctly, it is not possible to raise Variation magnitude permanently or gain new variations without increasing Scar magnitude or gaining new scars.<br /> But Scar magnitude can only be increased (or new Scar acquired) if the character has Instability damage.<br /> <br /> So if the character has no Instability damage, they cannot acquire new variations or increase existing variation magnitude. Is that correct ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T06:14:34-07:00","id":1490126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwhisper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1490099#post1490099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if the character has no Instability damage, they cannot acquire new variations or increase existing variation magnitude. Is that correct ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Barring the temporary increases Cephalists and Coactives can get from their Adaptations, yes, that's correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T13:51:41-07:00","id":1490925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1490126#post1490126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Barring the temporary increases Cephalists and Coactives can get from their Adaptations, yes, that's correct.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems a bit weird that the only way to improve a character's power is through a &quot;damage mechanic&quot; that everything else in the game pushes you to heal.<br /> I guess it's meant to avoid having a power fantasy game instead of an rpg with themes of body horror etc.<br /> <br /> Anyway, thank you for your answers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T15:49:09-07:00","id":1490941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwhisper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1490925#post1490925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems a bit weird that the only way to improve a character's power is through a &quot;damage mechanic&quot; that everything else in the game pushes you to heal.<br /> I guess it's meant to avoid having a power fantasy game instead of an rpg with themes of body horror etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Power and debility go hand-in-hand for the Remade; their transformation is unstable and wild, and every Variation is counterbalanced by a Scar. The most powerful Remade are also the ones with the most glaring weaknesses, and the ones most vulnerable to breaking down if they don't get ahead of their instability.<br /> <br /> It's also not like you're going to find yourself hurting for opportunities to develop enough instability to produce a Scar. You suffer instability just by <i>existing</i> at the beginning of every story, and more for just spending time (sessions) without pursuing Touchstones. Any instability at all, even just one minor point, is enough to develop a new permanent Scar dot.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-03T08:34:28-07:00","id":1492225,"title":"","content":"As a kind of follow-up question to my previous one:<br /> what's the rationale of gaining new Scars by <i>healing</i> Instability?<br /> <br /> The book describes Instability as a measure of &quot;how profoundly the Deviant\u2019s Scars affect her quality of life&quot;, and is strictly tied to her sense of self and how much she clings to humanity.<br /> By neglecting their Touchstones, Deviants neglect their ties with humanity, hence growing Instability which in turn worsen their Scars or creates new ones.<br /> This concept is quite clear.<br /> <br /> But I don't understand the &quot;other way around&quot;, i.e. why by developing a new Scar the Deviant can heal Instability?<br /> It doesn't make much sense to me that new Scars can be developed both by <i>gaining </i>Instability and <i>healing </i>it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-03T09:31:06-07:00","id":1492233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwhisper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1492225#post1492225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I don't understand the &quot;other way around&quot;, i.e. why by developing a new Scar the Deviant can heal Instability?<br /> It doesn't make much sense to me that new Scars can be developed both by <i>gaining </i>Instability and <i>healing </i>it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's gaining the Scar that's healing the Instability, not the other way around.<br /> <br /> It's a limited means of venting temporary Instability by normalizing it into a permanent Scar, which nevertheless will cause subsequent applications of that workaround to have more severe results until/unless the Scar is entangled with a Variation. It's like making peace with the fact that your house has a leaky roof that refuses to stay fixed instead of continuing to lose money trying to patch it; the permanent Scar is worse for the transformed than Instability, but it is <i>more stable.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-03T10:28:30-07:00","id":1492238,"title":"","content":"<i>edit:</i> I had a thing here, but on second thought I think the reasoning was wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 09-03-2022, 01:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-03T12:40:55-07:00","id":1492248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1492233#post1492233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it's gaining the Scar that's healing the Instability, not the other way around.<br /> <br /> It's a limited means of venting temporary Instability by normalizing it into a permanent Scar, which nevertheless will cause subsequent applications of that workaround to have more severe results until/unless the Scar is entangled with a Variation. It's like making peace with the fact that your house has a leaky roof that refuses to stay fixed instead of continuing to lose money trying to patch it; the permanent Scar is worse for the transformed than Instability, but it is <i>more stable.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>That was a nice way of putting it, thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-08T08:42:20-07:00","id":1492603,"title":"","content":"Persistent Scars, page 158: &quot;<i>A player may only combine them with Persistent Variations, except when a Deviation says otherwise.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> But Variations don't have a Persistent keyword. They have the <i>Perpetual </i>keyword.<br /> <br /> The activation method of a Variation can be Persistent, but the activation method is determined by the entangled Scar.<br /> So the quoted sentence wouldn't make sense: &quot;Persistent Scars can only be combined with Variations entangled with a Persistent Scar.&quot;<br /> <br /> Unless it's a typo and by Persistent Variations the authors meant Perpetual Variations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-08T10:39:13-07:00","id":1492606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwhisper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1492603#post1492603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Persistent Scars, page 158: &amp;quot;<i>A player may only combine them with Persistent Variations, except when a Deviation says otherwise.</i>&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> But Variations don't have a Persistent keyword. They have the <i>Perpetual </i>keyword.<br /> <br /> The activation method of a Variation can be Persistent, but the activation method is determined by the entangled Scar.<br /> So the quoted sentence wouldn't make sense: &amp;quot;Persistent Scars can only be combined with Variations entangled with a Persistent Scar.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Unless it's a typo and by Persistent Variations the authors meant Perpetual Variations?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's just reiterating the basics there because there are Deviations/Scars in both other activation methods that entangle a non-Persistent Varation with a Persistent Scar indirectly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-10T07:14:38-07:00","id":1492754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1492606#post1492606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's just reiterating the basics there because there are Deviations/Scars in both other activation methods that entangle a non-Persistent Varation with a Persistent Scar indirectly.</div> </div> </div> </div>So that means, for example, I can entangle Telekinesis with a Persistent Scar and use it at will, with no activation roll required, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-10T08:20:21-07:00","id":1492758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwhisper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1492754#post1492754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So that means, for example, I can entangle Telekinesis with a Persistent Scar and use it at will, with no activation roll required, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a Persistent Variation it is constantly available to you without having to activate it for the scene, yes. Telekinesis as a semi-specific example will still require rolls to <i>use</i>, because it's a Directed Variation, but that's a separate category of keyword from activation method.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-10T10:33:49-07:00","id":1492767,"title":"","content":"Notably Telekinesis is also Toggled, which means that even entangled with a Persistent Scar, it still requires an unrolled instant action to activate for the scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-19T13:08:15-08:00","id":1497559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1482476#post1482476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In that case, why not just go with the Symbiote Form? You really don't need to stat out the spirit to have it hang around in Twilight. A Bound's Geist only has a projection in Twilight and can't act independently at all, unless it's Unleashed.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, how I may try to adapt a &quot;Unleash&quot; to Deviant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-19T14:35:55-08:00","id":1497570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1497559#post1497559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, how I may try to adapt a &amp;quot;Unleash&amp;quot; to Deviant?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe you could use Involuntary Stimulus or Alternate Persona?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-19T23:39:26-08:00","id":1497611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1497559#post1497559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, how I may try to adapt a &quot;Unleash&quot; to Deviant?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, high-Magnitude Telekinesis hits a lot of the relevant points and there's plenty of Standard Deviations to model most of that Magnitude being balanced by lack of control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-23T12:36:43-08:00","id":1497936,"title":"","content":"What are some good roleplaying cues for a Deviant who has Superhuman Intelligence entangled with Bestial Mind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-23T16:02:18-08:00","id":1497952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1497936#post1497936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are some good roleplaying cues for a Deviant who has Superhuman Intelligence entangled with Bestial Mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly as having the intellect result in a feedback loop where simple concepts begin to become inconceivable. Or that for the mind to work on a superhuman level, it must have an intense focus on what it thinks about, and anything that disturbs it leads to an overload","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-25T12:12:01-08:00","id":1498046,"title":"","content":"Can I use Monstrous Transformation to &quot;power up&quot; a variation I already have? For example, if I had Superhuman Strength 2 and one of the variations tied to my Monstrous Transformation is Superhuman Strength 3, do I effectively have Superhuman Strength 5 while Monstrous Transformation is on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-25T12:38:52-08:00","id":1498047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1498046#post1498046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I use Monstrous Transformation to &quot;power up&quot; a variation I already have? For example, if I had Superhuman Strength 2 and one of the variations tied to my Monstrous Transformation is Superhuman Strength 3, do I effectively have Superhuman Strength 5 while Monstrous Transformation is on?</div> </div> </div> </div>You have Superhuman Strength 3. Monstrous Transformation is for activating multiple Variations at once as an Overt action, not for stacking Magnitude on Variations you already have by circumventing the &quot;each instance of a Variation that can be taken more than once does a different thing&quot; language common to those powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-28T21:02:12-08:00","id":1498267,"title":"","content":"One option for the dependency scar's common deviation allows for deviants to require something like large amounts of food. I was thinking, could I have the dependency scar make it so that a deviant was incapable of consuming certain things a human could and had to find other ways of getting the nutrition i.e. a carnivore Chimeric is incapable of digesting fruits and vegetables but still needs the nutrition from plants so they eat wild animals to get it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T22:45:47-08:00","id":1498815,"title":"","content":"Do Deviants count as Kin for Beasts? I think they should. They have a lot of conceptual overlap with Prometheans and Changelings, and those canonically count as Kin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-05T07:50:26-08:00","id":1498858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1498815#post1498815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Deviants count as Kin for Beasts? I think they should. They have a lot of conceptual overlap with Prometheans and Changelings, and those canonically count as Kin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably at the same level as mages","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-05T08:12:31-08:00","id":1498861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1498815#post1498815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Deviants count as Kin for Beasts? .</div> </div> </div> </div>Like most things with regard to Deviant, the answer probably depends on each Remade on an individual basis. While many will fall into the category of &quot;person who was turned into a monster&quot; you also have some who may never have been human to begin with, and at that point you may fall into the same bucket as Unchained. There are also some who will hardly be different than mortals with supernatural merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T11:49:51-08:00","id":1502404,"title":"","content":"Does the Holographic Projection variation only allow for visual illusions, or can I create fake smells, sounds, temperatures, etc? Also, can the variation be used to make objects invisible so long as you are in range i.e. making evidence at a crime scene invisible so that investigators can't see it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T12:55:23-08:00","id":1502415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1498815#post1498815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Deviants count as Kin for Beasts? I think they should. They have a lot of conceptual overlap with Prometheans and Changelings, and those canonically count as Kin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that the level of connection actually matters*, but Deviants would fall under the Descended from the Dark Mother category. The degree of change rendered by the Divergence is more on par with what a Durance does the people who become changelings.<br /> <br /> &quot;Is it Kin?&quot; is a very easy to thing to answer, with it's main contention being words of god not present in the text. For now, the metric is &quot;Is the character/person/entity in question actively supernatural that does not have roots in the God-Machine**?&quot; Unless you're talking a pure human with nothing magical or monstrous(it terms of physical/metaphysical quality) about them or anything that is what it is because of the God-Machine, it's Kin.<br /> <br /> *So far, the Fundamentally Human category is a semantic argument that has no actual bearing on the mechanics of Kinship, and seems to be there to handle people who have trouble grokking the Awakened or your friendly neighborhood telekinetic as monsters in the same vein as vampires, werewolves, and fairies. Whether the game should make a more meaningful distinction between the Dark Mother Descended category and the Fundamentally Human category or more meaningfully flatten the two together is an argument that probably should be had.<br /> **The main wrinkle in the argument is that Dave Brookshaw posited that the Abyss also probably shouldn't count on account of it's metaphysical nature being one of &quot;cannot have meaning imposed on it and will warp, twist, and destroy meaning introduced into it&quot;, which is actually a good argument, ruined by the fact that Beast has demonstrable Kinship with &quot;avatars&quot; of the Abyss(Acamoth and gulmoth, as the main example) by way of a Kinship Nightmare as text in the corebook. A Second Edition or a future supplement might weigh in and make it text, but for now, Only God-Machine related supernaturals have no Kinship with Beasts. The only other remaining argument is whether things like the Cursed or Destiny merits count as either metaphysics laid around a person or if they are made a part of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-07-2023, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T00:19:27-08:00","id":1502485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1502404#post1502404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the Holographic Projection variation only allow for visual illusions, or can I create fake smells, sounds, temperatures, etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can specifically create sounds, as demonstrated by the stated limitations and capabilities of its first and second Magnitudes. Even with the Magnitude 3 addition of tangibility to the illusion, I am not certain that qualities other than the stated audio-visual/hologram classification can be managed with Holographic Projection by default.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, can the variation be used to make objects invisible so long as you are in range i.e. making evidence at a crime scene invisible so that investigators can't see it. </div> </div> </div>It's a Directed Variation, meaning you have to be within forty yards of the thing you'd be covering up and you'd be <i>covering it up</i> while doing so; the power is very clearly additive, not subtractive, so you're not going to be able to literally make something invisible rather than applying a layer of camouflage over it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T17:34:09-08:00","id":1502973,"title":"","content":"Let's say I have a deviant with superhuman strength and a monstrous transformation that also grants superhuman strength.<br /> <br /> Do they stack (up to the usual maximum), or do you take the higher one while the transformation is active?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T19:36:29-08:00","id":1502988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1502973#post1502973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's say I have a deviant with superhuman strength and a monstrous transformation that also grants superhuman strength.<br /> <br /> Do they stack (up to the usual maximum), or do you take the higher one while the transformation is active?</div> </div> </div> </div>Take the higher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-22T14:22:15-08:00","id":1503703,"title":"","content":"The book explicitly recommends that you allow players to swap or combine Scars, but makes no mention of splitting or unentangling Scars. Does that mean that, by RAW, entangling two or more Variations with the same Scar means neither of them can ever reach 5 dots? Since the maximum Scar Magnitude is 5, which can only support Variation Magnitude 4 or less if it's entangled with more than one Variation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-22T20:13:34-08:00","id":1503725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1503703#post1503703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book explicitly recommends that you allow players to swap or combine Scars, but makes no mention of splitting or unentangling Scars. Does that mean that, by RAW, entangling two or more Variations with the same Scar means neither of them can ever reach 5 dots? Since the maximum Scar Magnitude is 5, which can only support Variation Magnitude 4 or less if it's entangled with more than one Variation.</div> </div> </div> </div>It means that if you have multiple Variations entangled with the same Scar, you would need to replace the Scar one of them is entangled with with a different one to increase the maximum Magnitude those Variations can reach.<br /> <br /> Not being able to maximize the Magnitude of a Variation is notably also a consequence of how Monstrous Transformation works, since that Variation's actual mechanical effect is &quot;activate multiple Variations as a single Toggled action at the cost of that action being Overt and making more of a splash than any one of them would have individually.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Splitting&quot; here entails replacement \u2014 the paragraph is about Scars in general, with the statement about Variations just specifying that if you change what Scars your character has they still need to meet the entangled Scar Magnitude requirements for any Variations they have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-26T11:01:37-08:00","id":1503954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1503725#post1503725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you would need to replace the Scar one of them is entangled with</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does it say you're allowed to do that? Because the paragraph I'm thinking of (&quot;Fused and Shifting Scars&quot;, p.111) reads:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the player feels her character has too many scars to reasonably play, or if a Scar seemed interesting at the time impedes her ability to have fun (or makes it less fun for everyone in the troup), the Storyteller may allow her to <b>replace a Scar with one of equal Magnitude</b> or to <b>fuse two or more Scars into a single Scar</b>. This must always result in a legal number of entangled Variations attached to each Scar. </div> </div> </div>The way I read that, if you have two 4-dot Variations entangled with a 5-dor Scar, you can swap that Scar for a different one, potentially changing the activation method, attributes etc. for both Variations, but there seems to be no allowance for switching one of the Variations to a different 4- or 5-dot Scar.<br /> <br /> (I would certainly allow a player to do that, but unless it's discussed somewhere else, I don't think it's RAW.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","user":"Terrorforge","date":". 02-26-2023, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-26T19:27:21-08:00","id":1503976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1503954#post1503954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where does it say you're allowed to do that? Because the paragraph I'm thinking of (&quot;Fused and Shifting Scars&quot;, p.111)</div> </div> </div> </div>The paragraph we are both talking about, is about Scars in general being changeable by the players and Storyteller to keep the game fun, and its specific note that this still requires a character's Variations to be entangled with their Scars in a mechanically legal fashion. It doesn't talk about splitting Scars because for the most part that is either legally impossible or else allows a character to lose Scar Magnitude. A character with five Magnitude 1 Variations entangled with a Magnitude 5 Scar doesn't get the option to ratchet down to having five Magnitude 1 Scars, but they could be allowed reassign however many of those Variations they needed to a second (or third, or fourth) Magnitude 5 Scar.<br /> <br /> It &quot;says&quot; it by inference from the fact that this is a paragraph about how if a character's Scar is interfering with the smooth and enjoyable execution of play then the Storyteller can let their player adjust the mechanical representation of that bit of their Scars. It would be nonsensical for this clear description of intent to still not allow you to disconnect two Controlled Scars from having the same activation cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-25T16:00:38-07:00","id":1506439,"title":"","content":"If I take Pyrokinesis 2 and Lash 2 and entangle them both with Unstable Variation 3, can I use my scar-free dot of Variation magnitude from my origin to apply that reduction to Unstable Variation? In which case it gets knocked down from magnitude 3 to 2?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-25T17:08:39-07:00","id":1506444,"title":"","content":"No, the scar free dot applies to your powers, not your scars. It could let you increase either of your powers to 3 though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-25T18:14:39-07:00","id":1506447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1506439#post1506439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I take Pyrokinesis 2 and Lash 2 and entangle them both with Unstable Variation 3, can I use my scar-free dot of Variation magnitude from my origin to apply that reduction to Unstable Variation? In which case it gets knocked down from magnitude 3 to 2?</div> </div> </div> </div>As ShadowcatX says, a dot of Scar-free Variation Magnitude is not a reduction in Scar Magnitude.<br /> <br /> Effectively, the Scar-free dot lets you treat a Variation as one Magnitude lower for the purposes of minimum entangled Scar Magnitude \u2014 you can have a one-dot Variation with no Scar attached (choosing its keywords at character creation and then presumably adhering to those same keywords if/when you need to entangle it with a Scar to raise its Magnitude), you can entangle a five-dot Variation with a five-dot Scar and still be able to entangle another Variation of up to Magnitude 4 with that Scar, and every little-v variation on that theme in-between.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T04:49:08-07:00","id":1509025,"title":"","content":"If a Deviant ruins a touchstones life to the point where said touchstone commits suicide, does it count as the Deviant killing said touchstone for the purposes of Willpower and Instability purposes or do Deviants have to do the killing themselves?<br /> <br /> Also, if multiple Deviants work together to kill a Shared conviction touchstone, do they all get the Willpower and Instability benefits or do the benefits only go to the one that does the killing? For example, if a group of Deviants beat a conviction touchstone to death, do they all get benefits, or does only the one who dealt the killing blow get them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T04:52:51-07:00","id":1509026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1509025#post1509025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Deviant ruins a touchstones life to the point where said touchstone commits suicide, does it count as the Deviant killing said touchstone for the purposes of Willpower and Instability purposes or do Deviants have to do the killing themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it depends on if the Deviant comes to the conclusion that it's their fault. One who rationalized away their complicity probably wouldn't, but one who blames themselves probably will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T05:49:56-07:00","id":1509029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1509026#post1509026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it depends on if the Deviant comes to the conclusion that it's their fault. One who rationalized away their complicity probably wouldn't, but one who blames themselves probably will.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, what do you think about the second paragraph?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T05:56:33-07:00","id":1509030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1509029#post1509029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, what do you think about the second paragraph?</div> </div> </div> </div>Aaaah... I'm mostly speculating here, I don't know Deviant well. But I'd say it depends on the scene. The group beating, where no-one knows who delivered the killing blow? I'd say the group as a whole gets it. One Deviant pulling the trigger while the rest watch? I'd say the trigger man gets it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T06:34:44-07:00","id":1509033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1509025#post1509025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Deviant ruins a touchstones life to the point where said touchstone commits suicide, does it count as the Deviant killing said touchstone for the purposes of Willpower and Instability purposes or do Deviants have to do the killing themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this something that has actually come up in a game or are you only theory crafting? Suicide is a touchy subject for a lot of people, and blaming someone for someone else's suicide (which is what the willpower / instability argument basically is) is a difficult topic beyond just normal suicide. It's ground I would be very hesitant to cover no matter and absolutely an area where, if you cover it at all, you should do so carefully, RAW on the situation be damned either way. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, if multiple Deviants work together to kill a Shared conviction touchstone, do they all get the Willpower and Instability benefits or do the benefits only go to the one that does the killing? For example, if a group of Deviants beat a conviction touchstone to death, do they all get benefits, or does only the one who dealt the killing blow get them? </div> </div> </div>If it's a teamwork effort, then I would say they all gain all the benefits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T15:02:17-07:00","id":1509318,"title":"","content":"Computer-Aided Processing explicitly states that Attribute dots in excess of 5 don't affect computations for Scar Power/Finesse/Resistance; do shifted Attribute ratings still affect calculations for Scars and Variations below that threshold?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T16:19:16-07:00","id":1509324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1509318#post1509318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Computer-Aided Processing explicitly states that Attribute dots in excess of 5 don't affect computations for Scar Power/Finesse/Resistance; do shifted Attribute ratings still affect calculations for Scars and Variations below that threshold?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems fine to me. There's a trade-off because you're moving dots around, so improving your Scar Finesse might mean decreasing your Scar Power or the like. And it's good to have an advantage to the power that moves dots around that isn't present in the power that just gives you more dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T16:52:03-07:00","id":1509327,"title":"","content":"The Hungerless power of the Anomalous Biology variation allows a deviant to survive without eating or drinking, but the deviant can still eat and drink if they want to. What Scar(s) and/or deviations could I take to create a deviant who was incapable of eating or drinking anything?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T17:04:26-07:00","id":1509328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1509327#post1509327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hungerless power of the Anomalous Biology variation allows a deviant to survive without eating or drinking, but the deviant can still eat and drink if they want to. What Scar(s) and/or deviations could I take to create a deviant who was incapable of eating or drinking anything?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would entirely depend on how you want it to manifest. You could take Bane to make them allergic to food, Sluggish Metabolism for heightened susceptibility to poisoning and disease, Sensory Deprivation to make them unable to taste Conspicuous Appearance or Silence for them not having a mouth, and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T11:09:12-07:00","id":1509501,"title":"","content":"Animal Transformation says you get the Physical Attributes of the creature you are turning into. How does this work for swarms? Are there guidelines for this anywhere? In this case, specifically a swarm of spiders for one of my players. They are specifically going to want to be making rolls in swarm form for a variety of tasks, so I need to figure out Attributes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T18:23:28-07:00","id":1509539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1509501#post1509501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Animal Transformation says you get the Physical Attributes of the creature you are turning into. How does this work for swarms? Are there guidelines for this anywhere? In this case, specifically a swarm of spiders for one of my players. They are specifically going to want to be making rolls in swarm form for a variety of tasks, so I need to figure out Attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pending clarification or examples to the contrary in the Clade Companion, the stats for a swarm are as described in the Swarm, Biting Swarm, and Lethal Swarm variants of Animal Transformation; the fact that there aren't guidelines for the Attributes of a swarm and a swarm without the capability to inflict damage is placed at the Magnitude where Variations tend to be balanced toward suggests to me that the intention is that a swarm of bugs/rats/tiny birds/etc is not capable of taking actions for which dice are rolled; analogous powers in other gamelines either use a variation on the character's normal Attributes or treat the character as a mobile hazard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T07:16:30-07:00","id":1509581,"title":"","content":"Does a Deviant's Progenitor have to be human, or can another supernatural produce a Deviant? Some examples of the latter would be a werewolf trying to force a First Change, a Mage trying to force an awakening, or a vampire bloodline whose embrace turns people into Deviants rather than more vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T07:41:31-07:00","id":1509583,"title":"","content":"Your progenitor can be anything that works for your story. If the story you all want to explore has vampires making deviants through the embrace, go for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T14:18:33-07:00","id":1509629,"title":"","content":"Can the storm caller variation summon acid rain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T14:48:04-07:00","id":1509630,"title":"","content":"Acid Rain isn't covered by the rules per se, but I can see that as an excuse to have rain considered a higher level environmental threat but I wouldn't give it anything special above and beyond the basic rules for extreme environmental threats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T18:26:04-07:00","id":1509670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1509581#post1509581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does a Deviant's Progenitor have to be human, or can another supernatural produce a Deviant? Some examples of the latter would be a werewolf trying to force a First Change, a Mage trying to force an awakening, or a vampire bloodline whose embrace turns people into Deviants rather than more vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Divergence is specifically produced by forms of power that don't have a guiding magical force behind them like Luna or the God-Machine or a vampire; different splats tend to have their own variations on &quot;your soul cracked open and stuff's gone wrong with it&quot; (e.g. the Enraptured, the Rampant, the Broken Souls) and, like Promethean 1e points out for demiurges, better-understood types of monster tend to have more readily available ways to make other monsters than the unreliable and poorly-understood process of engineering a Deviant who will survive the Divergence and not go Feral from failure to form connections. Thematically, the game is built around Baselines exploiting magic (or science, or spiritualism) for power at the expense of other people's humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T19:21:58-07:00","id":1510011,"title":"","content":"What scars would I take to represent a Deviant who has asthma?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T19:39:36-07:00","id":1510013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1510011#post1510011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What scars would I take to represent a Deviant who has asthma?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends what you mean by that. Suppression (Stamina) or the lower Magnitudes of Genetic Disorder might fill the role, as might certain varieties of Bane or Native Environment, but the important question is what mechanical and narrative complications you want the character to have from the Scar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T19:46:33-07:00","id":1510016,"title":"","content":"Also, while we are on the subject of disabilities, what scars could represent artificial limbs (realistic ones not sci fi ones)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T20:03:00-07:00","id":1510018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1510016#post1510016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, while we are on the subject of disabilities, what scars could represent artificial limbs (realistic ones not sci fi ones)?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're asking for Scars relating to missing or limited limbs and senses, that's Missing Limb and Sensory Deprivation, respectively. If you're asking about Scars that can represent having obvious artificial limbs that serve as an identifying feature, Conspicuous Appearance at low Magnitudes can fill that role. If you're asking about just <i>having </i>artificial limbs, that's not a Scar unless it's intrinsic enough to the Deviant's condition to hang Variations off of by stemming from the Instability of their soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T06:56:14-07:00","id":1510198,"title":"","content":"I know that the Rapid Healing variation at Magnitude 5 allows a deviant to come back to life except for Instability, but how would I go about creating a Deviant who can still be killed by other ways? For example, a demon blooded Deviant who can revive themselves, but will stay dead if killed by a Bane of holy water.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T07:55:36-07:00","id":1510201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1510198#post1510198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that the Rapid Healing variation at Magnitude 5 allows a deviant to come back to life except for Instability, but how would I go about creating a Deviant who can still be killed by other ways? For example, a demon blooded Deviant who can revive themselves, but will stay dead if killed by a Bane of holy water.</div> </div> </div> </div>By having a commensurately powerful Bane.<br /> <br /> If a Bane has a base Magnitude of 4 (or a base Magnitude of 2 for a Bane that deals lethal damage to things without the Scar) then the damage it deals can't be healed by healing Variations, since it's damage caused by a Scar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T16:40:20-07:00","id":1510287,"title":"","content":"Is there a rule in the book that explains what happens if a Scar and a Variation are in conflict?<br /> <br /> The specific case is Frozen Heart (-3 untrained penalty for social skills) and Omnicompetent (no untrained penalty).<br /> <br /> It is only specifically stated that Scar drawbacks affect Entangled Variations, so I have (temporarily) ruled that Omnicompetent is unaffected and negates the untrained penalties as stated (as the player did not Entangle the two together), but I am curious if there is a rule specifically indicating what to do with this sort of conflict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T19:03:07-07:00","id":1510302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1510287#post1510287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a rule in the book that explains what happens if a Scar and a Variation are in conflict?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's the &quot;Choosing Scars&quot; sidebar on p173 as far as advice goes, and the general precedent seems to be that Scars take precedent in situations where that wouldn't completely negate the Variation's whole effect (i.e. if you've got Anomalous Biology [Tireless] it doesn't make sense to allow the character to get Scar Magnitude from Dependency [Fatigued]).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The specific case is Frozen Heart (-3 untrained penalty for social skills) and Omnicompetent (no untrained penalty). </div> </div> </div>I'd default to Frozen Heart applying the penalty here, because Omnicompetence negating the untrained penalty still applies to other categories and once you're past Magnitude 1 the Variation can circumvent the penalty by just temporarily having dots in the Skill you're using. You could also, if preferred, say that Omnicompetence 1 applies since Frozen Heart 2 still has another effect even without untrained penalties, but that's to taste.<br /> <br /> <br /> Speaking of fatigue: I've lost my advance copy PDF for comparison, but should the text of Hemophilia 5 be read as meaning that Hemophilia 4 normally gives you the Fatigued Condition if you take damage <i>in Health boxes that cause wound penalties</i>, as the rest of the pre-Magnitude 5 effects, or read exactly as written to apply the Fatigued Condition at the end of any scene where you took any damage at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Fixing a typo and adding an extra line break. 04-30-2023, 10:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T01:39:23-07:00","id":1510334,"title":"","content":"Thank you. Helpful points, particularly the sidebar.<br /> <br /> As to Hemophilia, I believe the Fatigued condition is the same at both Magnitude 4 and 5. It took re-reading the Scar several times, but I believe the change in Magnitude 5 is to the bleeding effect that 4 inherits from 3.<br /> <br /> That is:<br /> Hemophilia 4 gives: Fatigue at the end of the scene whenever you took damage <b>and </b>also causes bleeding if you take damage in a box that gives a wound penalty.<br /> Hemophilia 5 gives: Fatigue at the end of the scene where you took damage <b>and </b>also causes bleeding whenever you take any damage at all.<br /> <br /> So the Fatigue is the same. The &quot;any damage at all&quot; applies to what 4 inherits from 2 and 3: the bleeding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T12:21:27-07:00","id":1510904,"title":"","content":"How can I create a radioactive deviant that has to wear a lead suit to protect other people from themselves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T13:00:46-07:00","id":1510908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1510904#post1510904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can I create a radioactive deviant that has to wear a lead suit to protect other people from themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bioluminescence 5, possibly with Wild Variation if you want radiation that doesn't glow, definitely with Relentless Variation if you're going the Persistent route rather than Involuntary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T15:53:58-07:00","id":1510923,"title":"","content":"I have a number of questions in regards to touchstones:<br /> <br /> 1: If a deviant's touchstone is pregnant, can the deviant take the baby and the mother as separate touchstones?<br /> <br /> 2: Can a pregnant deviant take their unborn baby as a touchstone?<br /> <br /> 3: Can a deviant destroy their conviction touchstones indirectly and still get the benefits? For example, if a deviant hires a hitman to kill a conviction touchstone for them, does the deviant count as being the killer for willpower and instability purposes?<br /> <br /> 4: Can a deviant help their loyalty touchstone indirectly and still get the benefits? For example, if a deviant kills their loyalty touchstones stalker, do they gain benefits?<br /> <br /> 5: Can a deviant have a loyalty touchstone that hates them or a conviction touchstone that loves them? For the first, an example would be a loyalty touchstone that holds a grudge against the deviant, while for the latter an example would be a conviction touchstone that is a yandere.<br /> <br /> 6: Can a deviant have a group of people that collectively count as one touchstone? For example, a polyamourous deviant whose lovers all serve as one touchstone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27678,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","user":"cybirddude","date":". 05-06-2023, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T17:49:20-07:00","id":1510938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1510923#post1510923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1: If a deviant's touchstone is pregnant, can the deviant take the baby and the mother as separate touchstones?<br /> <br /> 2: Can a pregnant deviant take their unborn baby as a touchstone?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though the unborn child does not have enough of an independent existence from the parent carrying it to justify the kinds of things that a Loyalty Touchstone mechanically affects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3: Can a deviant destroy their conviction touchstones indirectly and still get the benefits? For example, if a deviant hires a hitman to kill a conviction touchstone for them, does the deviant count as being the killer for willpower and instability purposes? </div> </div> </div>Does this sound like the sort of thing that fulfills the drive of a stat called <i>Conviction</i>?<br /> <br /> Like, sure, you almost definitely don't need to lethally end the Touchstone's existence with your hands around their throat, but the story beat regaining Stability in this way represents involves something that the deviant can actually identify themselves by. Riding along with the hitman or having the Touchstone on a video call when the hit comes in or controlling the hitman with Variations or otherwise being able to be there and involved when the destruction happens has firmer ground to stand on, but giving a guy with a gun money to break into a secure compound that produced a sewer mutant like yourself does not feed into the narrative of a burning need for vengeance the way dropping a building on your creator, burning them alive, or even just shooting them after the guy you hired to kidnap them delivers them to you does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4: Can a deviant help their loyalty touchstone indirectly and still get the benefits? For example, if a deviant kills their loyalty touchstones stalker, do they gain benefits? </div> </div> </div>&quot;Take a risk or suffer for a Loyalty Touchstone&quot; or &quot;perform some service for a Loyalty Touchstone&quot; both jive with this, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5: Can a deviant have a loyalty touchstone that hates them or a conviction touchstone that loves them? For the first, an example would be a loyalty touchstone that holds a grudge against the deviant, while for the latter an example would be a conviction touchstone that is a yandere. </div> </div> </div>I mean, yes? One of the defining things about the Touchstone provided by Living Progenitor is that it can flip categories entirely instead of Wavering, which is itself just a more specific mechanic to the ability for any deviant to change the category of a Touchstone and all the material about Touchstones generally concerns the deviant's feelings on the relationship.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6: Can a deviant have a group of people that collectively count as one touchstone? For example, a polyamourous deviant whose lovers all serve as one touchstone. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Some Broken forge ties with an object, place, or organization, but these are always concrete and localized \u2014 something that can be threatened or destroyed by a single actor in a single time and place, whether with a gun or an explosive.&quot;<br /> <br /> The ability to have an organization as a Touchstone is not a way to have a Touchstone with extra lives, it's a way to make <i>a group</i> with the capacity to be put in danger one of the things holding your Stability together. Any collective Touchstone should account for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T17:57:00-07:00","id":1510940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1510938#post1510938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel as though the unborn child does not have enough of an independent existence from the parent carrying it to justify the kinds of things that a Loyalty Touchstone mechanically affects.<br /> <br /> Does this sound like the sort of thing that fulfills the drive of a stat called <i>Conviction</i>?<br /> <br /> Like, sure, you almost definitely don't need to lethally end the Touchstone's existence with your hands around their throat, but the story beat regaining Stability in this way represents involves something that the deviant can actually identify themselves by. Riding along with the hitman or having the Touchstone on a video call when the hit comes in or controlling the hitman with Variations or otherwise being able to be there and involved when the destruction happens has firmer ground to stand on, but giving a guy with a gun money to break into a secure compound that produced a sewer mutant like yourself does not feed into the narrative of a burning need for vengeance the way dropping a building on your creator, burning them alive, or even just shooting them after the guy you hired to kidnap them delivers them to you does.<br /> <br /> &quot;Take a risk or suffer for a Loyalty Touchstone&quot; or &quot;perform some service for a Loyalty Touchstone&quot; both jive with this, yes.<br /> <br /> I mean, yes? One of the defining things about the Touchstone provided by Living Progenitor is that it can flip categories entirely instead of Wavering, which is itself just a more specific mechanic to the ability for any deviant to change the category of a Touchstone and all the material about Touchstones generally concerns the deviant's feelings on the relationship.<br /> <br /> &quot;Some Broken forge ties with an object, place, or organization, but these are always concrete and localized \u2014 something that can be threatened or destroyed by a single actor in a single time and place, whether with a gun or an explosive.&quot;<br /> <br /> The ability to have an organization as a Touchstone is not a way to have a Touchstone with extra lives, it's a way to make <i>a group</i> with the capacity to be put in danger one of the things holding your Stability together. Any collective Touchstone should account for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>So for 6, would multiple lovers count as one touchstone if they all lived together? An enemy could simply bomb their house or shoot all of them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T18:51:04-07:00","id":1510944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1510940#post1510940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So for 6, would multiple lovers count as one touchstone if they all lived together? An enemy could simply bomb their house or shoot all of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is &quot;the deviant's lovers&quot; an organization that can concretely be brought to an end, or is it reasonable to assume that Alice, Bob, and Cal could not be be Ship of Theseus'd out of the quadrouple one by one and still leave Devin the deviant with a functional anchor to humanity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-08T20:57:20-07:00","id":1511103,"title":"","content":"Two questions regarding Genotypals: <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bIs a possible for a Genotypal to be a deviant from birth, in the sense that they became deviants in the womb rather than later in life?<br /> <br /> Aside from reincarnation shenanigans, how can a Genotypal be Self-Made?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-08T22:27:09-07:00","id":1511107,"title":"","content":"Swallow a mutagen of your own concoction","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T04:50:35-07:00","id":1511117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1511103#post1511103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bIs a possible for a Genotypal to be a deviant from birth, in the sense that they became deviants in the womb rather than later in life?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the larger setting metaphysics, the human soul appears at birth and Scars and Variations are symptoms of the soul being broken. In practical terms, literally nobody is going to be playing an unborn fetus, but the book says that while Genotypal Remade often discover their Variations in adolescence the trigger for their powers manifesting might come earlier or later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Aside from reincarnation shenanigans, how can a Genotypal be Self-Made? </div> </div> </div>Same methods an Autourgic might use with a greater emphasis on the criteria that would make a Genotypal, like tapping into a family curse or discovering and leveraging the notes of a destroyed conspiracy who put the markers in place for them to undergo the Divergence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T14:53:40-07:00","id":1511411,"title":"","content":"Can a deviant have a loyalty touchstone that is a friendly rival (i.e. a romantic rival who will accept being the loser, a rival business that engages in healthy competition, a rival martial artist who inspired the deviant to improve themself)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T17:55:52-07:00","id":1511419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1511411#post1511411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a deviant have a loyalty touchstone that is a friendly rival (i.e. a romantic rival who will accept being the loser, a rival business that engages in healthy competition, a rival martial artist who inspired the deviant to improve themself)?</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the example Loyalty Touchstones is &quot;The Frenemy,&quot; a rival whose blurb includes the statement that &quot;Competing with him made you try harder, and you both became experts in your field.&quot; Yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T13:38:25-07:00","id":1511736,"title":"","content":"Making sure I've correctly understood how Channeling a Variation through Lash works:<br /> <br /> \u2022 You roll to attack with the Lash as normal, and if the attack deals the necessary amount of damage based on the damage type of the Lash and the target's Armor, the secondary Variation is reflexively activated without a roll.<br /> \u2022 For the purposes of determining if the target is subject to the effects of the Channeled Variation, the target rolls the relevant Resistance pool contested against the Lash's rolled successes.<br /> \u2022 If the Lash targets multiple characters (i.e. through Blasting, Burst, Full-Auto, or Circle Strike), it can affect up to the normal maximum number of characters that Directed Variation normally could, and each target contests the successes as normal.<br /> \u2022 Channeling a Variation through a ranged Lash can thus allow it to reach further and affect multiple targets faster than the normal Directed Variation ranges, as well as potentially using a different dicepool than the secondary Variation would use by itself, with the principal tradeoff being that the Lash needs to be entangled with another Scar (or the same Scar as the secondary Variation, which caps the Magnitude of the secondary at 4 at most).<br /> <br /> Is that all correct?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T15:10:42-07:00","id":1511922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1511736#post1511736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making sure I've correctly understood how Channeling a Variation through Lash works:<br /> <br /> \u2022 You roll to attack with the Lash as normal, and if the attack deals the necessary amount of damage based on the damage type of the Lash and the target's Armor, the secondary Variation is reflexively activated without a roll.<br /> \u2022 For the purposes of determining if the target is subject to the effects of the Channeled Variation, the target rolls the relevant Resistance pool contested against the Lash's rolled successes.<br /> \u2022 If the Lash targets multiple characters (i.e. through Blasting, Burst, Full-Auto, or Circle Strike), it can affect up to the normal maximum number of characters that Directed Variation normally could, and each target contests the successes as normal.<br /> \u2022 Channeling a Variation through a ranged Lash can thus allow it to reach further and affect multiple targets faster than the normal Directed Variation ranges, as well as potentially using a different dicepool than the secondary Variation would use by itself, with the principal tradeoff being that the Lash needs to be entangled with another Scar (or the same Scar as the secondary Variation, which caps the Magnitude of the secondary at 4 at most).<br /> <br /> Is that all correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>This matches my reading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-22T13:03:14-07:00","id":1512378,"title":"","content":"Could a Deviant have a conviction touchstone that they don't want to kill, but want to live in misery? For example, the deviant might nurse the touchstone back to health when they are sick, or stop them from killing themselves, but only to make them miserable in ways such has driving the touchstone to poverty, isolating the touchstone from their friends and family, enslavement, torture, rape, etc.<br /> <br /> In addition, would tormenting a conviction touchstone count as pursuing a conviction touchstone for willpower and instability purposes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-22T19:16:52-07:00","id":1512397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1512378#post1512378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could a Deviant have a conviction touchstone that they don't want to kill, but want to live in misery? For example, the deviant might nurse the touchstone back to health when they are sick, or stop them from killing themselves, but only to make them miserable in ways such has driving the touchstone to poverty, isolating the touchstone from their friends and family, enslavement, torture, rape, etc.<br /> <br /> In addition, would tormenting a conviction touchstone count as pursuing a conviction touchstone for willpower and instability purposes?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I may make an observation about the way your posts have collectively been going, It seems like you have a overall interest in just how terrible you can have a character be and still have it be mechanically...permitted. If that's the case, I would suggest just making an overarching question about it in the Ask a Simple Question thread. If not, you might want to rethink your presentations.<br /> <br /> Anyways, RAW would suggest this is arguably viable for the purposes of pursuing the conviction for Willpower/Instability purposes....so long as there's an endgame to it. The Causes section clause about furthering a Touchstone or suffering Instability implies there's no such thing as a holding pattern (Hey, like over in Werewolf), and Loyalty is the place long, affirmative relationships-Convictions are about solutions, however small, to the ongoing problems of the Conspiracies in the Web of Pain. Sure, that might include dropping people into the Pit of Eternal Torment and No Escape, We Promise, but the incentive to resolve Conviction through murder is motivated by the fact that it's the most reliable way of ensuring they don't get to keep contributing to the Web, where as imprisonment requires resources to be kept perpetual, resources a Renegade is unlikely to be able to keep supplying for long given the target they have on their back.<br /> <br /> Also of note, in that vein, is that any Deviant trying to game the system of their Instability through imprisonment (or worse) is increasingly unlikely to keep their allies. A lot of Deviants, even if they have burning hatred for the actors of Conspiracies, also take issue with the sort of actions that Remade them, and that often includes imprisonment and torture-nevermind what Baseline allies are going to feel about it. A willingness to explore enslavement and rape as a means of action against them just exacerbates the problem, and continues to ensure that a Deviant interested in this violation as their coping mechanism is rapidly going to start losing the resources for doing.<br /> <br /> And of course, none of this is addressing the issues of such an interested character with players at the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T19:50:07-07:00","id":1512929,"title":"","content":"Some Body Snatcher questions:<br /> <br /> 1. Do the Magnitude 4 effects require you to first be riding the victim's senses with the Magnitude 1 effect before you take over their body for the scene, as the Magnitude 2 and 3 effects imply is required for their respective effects? If so, can this be taken to mean that using Body Swap multiple times in one scene (transferring your consciousness to a new target's body) effectively leaves your body comatose and intermittently occupied by whoever you've swapped with, with every previous swap returning to their own body once you've moved to a different body? If not, does using the Body Swap effect sequentially put each new target in the body of the previous target until the end of the scene?<br /> <br /> 2. Are Persistent Perpetual versions of Variations affecting the character's Attributes, Skills, and internal Mental Merits (i.e. Superhuman Attribute and Hyper-Competence) an exception to Body Snatcher's stipulation that you can't use your other Variations in a stolen body? If so, would the same exceptions apply to Controlled or Involuntary forms of those Variations? What about Computer-Aided Processing and Omnicompetence, whether Toggled or non-Persistent? If not, does this mean that e.g. a Psychic with Superhuman Intelligence could drop from Intelligence 8 to Intelligence 1 while operating in a borrowed body?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T18:13:11-07:00","id":1513348,"title":"","content":"I'm revisiting a character concept: Ray was partially Spirit-Claimed by a void spirit. He's been physically transformed, but most of the time he's invisible, or as he describes it, &quot;technically not completely existing.&quot; Right now, he's got Relentless/Suppressible Camouflage 3 entangled with Power Failure (Main Scar) and Concentration (Secondary Scar for Suppressible). I'm thinking of applying the Disfiguring Scar Deviation, so when his Camouflage fails, or he reveals himself, it's Overt. Relentless Variation specifies +1 Magnitude if persistence would cause problems, specifically mentioning Camo 3+ as an example. Disfiguring Scar gives +1 Magnitude to the scar it's attached to, and I'd say it'd make both PF and Concentration Overt.<br /> <br /> How do I work out the final magnitudes of Camouflage, Power Failure, and Concentration? If you were the Storyteller, would you allow this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T18:59:34-07:00","id":1513351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1513348#post1513348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm revisiting a character concept: Ray was partially Spirit-Claimed by a void spirit. He's been physically transformed, but most of the time he's invisible, or as he describes it, &quot;technically not completely existing.&quot; Right now, he's got Relentless/Suppressible Camouflage 3 entangled with Power Failure (Main Scar) and Concentration (Secondary Scar for Suppressible). I'm thinking of applying the Disfiguring Scar Deviation, so when his Camouflage fails, or he reveals himself, it's Overt. Relentless Variation specifies +1 Magnitude if persistence would cause problems, specifically mentioning Camo 3+ as an example. Disfiguring Scar gives +1 Magnitude to the scar it's attached to, and I'd say it'd make both PF and Concentration Overt.<br /> <br /> How do I work out the final magnitudes of Camouflage, Power Failure, and Concentration? If you were the Storyteller, would you allow this?</div> </div> </div> </div>The entire construction is mechanically illegal in the first place because Power Failure is not a Persistent Scar. Which Persistent Scar you replace Power Failure with in turn affects whether it's a valid subject for Disfiguring Scar, and as the secondary Scar Concentration is specifically the same Magnitude as the Persistent Scar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T19:20:19-07:00","id":1513352,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the correction. While I appreciate the flexibility they're going for in the system, it does get easy to confuse yourself, sometimes.<br /> <br /> So, new version to be checked:<br /> Variation: Camouflage 3 (Relentless/Suppressible +0?)<br /> Primary Scar: Dependency 2, (Disfiguring Scar for +1 and to make it Overt)<br /> Secondary Scar: Concentration 3 (made Overt by Disfiguring Scar)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10118,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","user":"BronzeDog","date":".  Added alternate version 05-30-2023, 11:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T07:18:06-07:00","id":1513531,"title":"","content":"Giving some more thought on pseudo-Claimed as Coactive Deviants, and currently focused on appropriate Scars.<ul><li>Bane is pretty easily adapted to represent the spirit's Bane.</li> <li>Subliminal Conditioning seems like it could work as a Ban at lower levels, though it gets more specific to controlling at higher levels.</li> <li>Dependency could be on Essence, where the skill roll represents finding a Locus or appropriately resonant location (Wits+Occult) or making an area resonant.</li> <li>Philia from the Devoted Companion might represent the spirit's overriding drive to harvest essence through the compulsion.</li> <li>Alternate Persona could represent an incomplete union, where the spirit and human half each have their own agenda.</li> <li>Conspicuous Appearance would be appropriate for sufficiently monstrous transformations as a result of the partial claiming.</li> <li>Phobia could represent a Ban that requires the spirit to flee certain situations.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T08:20:25-07:00","id":1513534,"title":"","content":"2 Questions about maniticores:<br /> <br /> 1: Can a deviant with the manticore companion merit loan their manticore to someone else? An example would be a parent deviant lending their manticore to their children while they are away.<br /> <br /> 2: Can symbiote manticores only be used by humans and deviants, or can other supernaturals, such as vampires, werewolves, changelings, etc. also use them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T15:56:47-07:00","id":1513576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1513534#post1513534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2 Questions about maniticores:<br /> <br /> 1: Can a deviant with the manticore companion merit loan their manticore to someone else? An example would be a parent deviant lending their manticore to their children while they are away.<br /> <br /> 2: Can symbiote manticores only be used by humans and deviants, or can other supernaturals, such as vampires, werewolves, changelings, etc. also use them.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Sure. Doing so basically &quot;taps it out&quot; until you retrieve it. A long enough period of loaning it out might warrant a Sanctity of Merits moment.<br /> 2) Sure, though being an entity outside of the paradigm should be a thing to consider for the character and how they interact with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T16:25:26-07:00","id":1513579,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't allow a symbiot manticore to bestow variations to a person with a major template. A minor template though, I might go for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T19:30:07-07:00","id":1513598,"title":"","content":"Since the core rulebook says that multiple Deviants can react differently based on physical, mental, and spiritual state and some forms of divergence are spiritual and/or mystical in nature, would it be possible for a deviants divergence to be controlled by things like:<br /> <br /> 1: Which of the seven deadly sins they are most guilty if.<br /> 2: Zodiac Signs.<br /> 3: Caste<br /> 4: Virginity<br /> 5: Karma","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T19:46:27-07:00","id":1513599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1513598#post1513598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the core rulebook says that multiple Deviants can react differently based on physical, mental, and spiritual state and some forms of divergence are spiritual and/or mystical in nature, would it be possible for a deviants divergence to be controlled by things like:<br /> <br /> 1: Which of the seven deadly sins they are most guilty if.<br /> 2: Zodiac Signs.<br /> 3: Caste<br /> 4: Virginity<br /> 5: Karma</div> </div> </div> </div>1. There are more than seven, but sure.<br /> 2. More influenced by the stars, but sure. The signs only exists as an idea, so you have to account for that.*<br /> 3. Only exists as an idea, so you have to account for that.*<br /> 4. Only exists as an idea, so you have to account for that.*<br /> 5. Sure.<br /> <br /> Sometimes the catalyst for Divergence is that the person being Remade flipped a tails last time they flipped a coin, so.<br /> <br /> *That said, the Temenos/Bright Dream is right there, so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T20:48:13-07:00","id":1513603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1513352#post1513352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, new version to be checked:<br /> Variation: Camouflage 3 (Relentless/Suppressible +0?)<br /> Primary Scar: Dependency 2, (Disfiguring Scar for +1 and to make it Overt)<br /> Secondary Scar: Concentration 3 (made Overt by Disfiguring Scar)</div> </div> </div> </div>You may be able to get away with a base Magnitude of 1 on Dependency through Relentless, as initially surmised, though how you intend to make it obvious to observers when Ray's missed a dose then becomes a necessary narrative exercise.<br /> <br /> Important follow-up question re: intention: what makes Ray re-appearing Overt? Because as a Toggled effect Camouflage normally can be ended before the end of the scene to no especial consequence for conspiracy surveillance rolls, so it's obviously not just &quot;a person has appeared where previously there was not a visible one.&quot;\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1513534#post1513534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2: Can symbiote manticores only be used by humans and deviants, or can other supernaturals, such as vampires, werewolves, changelings, etc. also use them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Manticore Companion Merit or conspiracy icons are the primary means of modeling symbionts. The former has a prerequisite of &quot;Deviant&quot; and the latter is the product of a conspiracy of Baselines and Deviants, the latter of whom the Symbiont section says can use symbionts if they haven't physically diverged too much (from the &quot;human host&quot; model indicated as the target user of a symbiont in the second sentence of the section).<br /> <br /> Vampires are undead, werewolves are excessively alive, changelings may well have nonsense anatomy under the Mask, and the fact that long-term symbiont use can trigger a Divergence (i.e. crack your soul open) suggests that in the circumstance where this hookup has managed to happen it will create a unique result best determined by the needs of the story or more depressingly trigger analogous circumstances like becoming one of the Enraptured/Broken Souls/Rampant/Petrificati/etc.<br /> <br /> They <i>are</i> notionally valid subjects for the Sacred Flesh Variation, but that's at a remove from &quot;integrate a magical animal into your human biology for first-and-a-half-hand access to superpowers.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T12:09:45-07:00","id":1513884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1513603#post1513603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You may be able to get away with a base Magnitude of 1 on Dependency through Relentless, as initially surmised, though how you intend to make it obvious to observers when Ray's missed a dose then becomes a necessary narrative exercise.<br /> <br /> Important follow-up question re: intention: what makes Ray re-appearing Overt? Because as a Toggled effect Camouflage normally can be ended before the end of the scene to no especial consequence for conspiracy surveillance rolls, so it's obviously not just &quot;a person has appeared where previously there was not a visible one.&quot;\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>For Relentless/Suppressible Camouflage, I'm going for is that Ray's been physically changed enough that it's quite notable when he reveals himself in front of other people, but not as extreme as Conspicuous Appearance. Disfiguring Scar seemed like an appropriate Deviation to use. For his Scars in general, I'm going for the idea that he's got some supernatural baggage from being an unusual Spirit-Claimed.<ul><li>I originally went with Power Failure thinking there could be places where his invisibility automatically fails, namely those with a resonance that opposes void or zero, such as abundance or large numbers, forcing him to stay away from places that are regularly crowded unless he could disguise his changes.</li> <li>I thought of Dependency next, where he has to seek out Loci or other resonant places to harvest essence. One idea I had for a quick fix was that he could make a large painting that would alter the local resonance, which could leave a trail for any conspiracy familiar with his art style.</li> <li>I might consider Conspicuous Appearance if I can figure out ways to keep it from getting too high. Then again, I might just need to bite the bullet and accept that he might end up looking more monstrous spirit-thing than human at some point.</li> </ul>I'm open to other suggestions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T19:18:54-07:00","id":1513907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1513884#post1513884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Relentless/Suppressible Camouflage, I'm going for is that Ray's been physically changed enough that it's quite notable when he reveals himself in front of other people, but not as extreme as Conspicuous Appearance.</div> </div> </div> </div>That feels like a weird line to draw, because the lowest level of Conspicuous Appearance is stuff like six-fingered hands or heterochromia and Magnitude 2 bumps that up to the level of glowing eyes or uncanny valley mannerisms; Conspicuous Appearance being Overt likewise means that Relentless Variation becomes a +1 Deviation with Camouflage 3 and so there's no need for the Scar to reach the point of Notoriety at base.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T11:46:25-07:00","id":1514214,"title":"","content":"The Misfortune Scar has a Deviation that causes bad luck to a Deviant's Loyalty touchstones and cohort. Can said bad luck extend to the friends, associates, benefactors etc. and can the variation give good luck to the Loyalty touchstone's/cohort's enemies? Some examples of what I mean.<br /> 1. A hunter cell Loyalty touchstone ends up being fed wrong info from a spy.<br /> 2. A hunter targeting the Deviant's supernatural touchstones ends up finding a bunch of useful clues.<br /> 3. A Devoted's superior hires a prostitute that turns out to be a Renegade with the Telepathy Variation.<br /> 4. The Devoted's conspiracy ends up kidnapping the beloved child of a powerful supernatural figure (i.e. a werewolf Alpha, a vampire Prince, an Apex Beast etc.)<br /> 5. A cohort member's child is killed/injured/hospitalized by a creep who takes rejection extremely poorly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27678,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","user":"cybirddude","date":". 06-08-2023, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T12:26:54-07:00","id":1514224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1514214#post1514214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Misfortune Scar has a Deviation that causes bad luck to a Deviant's Loyalty touchstones and cohort. Can said bad luck extend to the friends, associates, benefactors etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not unless those people are also Loyalty Touchstones and/or members of your cohort.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and can the variation give good luck to the Loyalty touchstone's/cohort's enemies? </div> </div> </div>That's how the bad luck options work when they aren't directly messing with the outcomes of your (or you cohort's) actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T13:16:51-07:00","id":1514233,"title":"","content":"The book mentions that deivants can take items , organizations, and locations as touchstones. Would the following examples be qualify as touchstones?<br /> 1: A particular translation of a holy text; furthering the touchstone involves reading or meditating on said text, and Stubborn resolve would allow them to resist breaking said text's commandments.<br /> 2: A bakery; furthering the touchstone would involve supporting it (i.e. donating money, advertising, sabotaging rivals etc.) , and Stubborn resolve would allow the deviant fo resist actions that would hurt the business in some way (i.e. revealing secret recipes, giving the owners bad advice, supporting a rival business etc.).<br /> 3: A martial arts dojo; supporting the touchstone would involve helping the students and/or teachers in some way (promoting the dojo, helping with teaching the students, sabotaging rival dojos), and stubborn resolve would allow the deviant to resist betraying the dojo.<br /> 4: A small group of con artists; supporting the touchstone would involve making sure the con artists prosper and aren't caught, and stubborn resolve would allow them to resist doing anything that would expose expose them or put them out of business.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T21:40:44-07:00","id":1514272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1514233#post1514233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book mentions that deivants can take items , organizations, and locations as touchstones. Would the following examples be qualify as touchstones?<br /> 1: A particular translation of a holy text;</div> </div> </div> </div>Not unless that translation is a concrete and localized thing that can be destroyed by a single actor in a single time and place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2: A bakery; </div> </div> </div>Sure.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3: A martial arts dojo; </div> </div> </div>Sure.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4: A small group of con artists; </div> </div> </div>See <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1510938#post1510938\">prior discussion</a> about how having a group as a Touchstone means <i>the group</i> is the thing anchoring the deviant's Stability.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> furthering the touchstone involves reading or meditating on said text, and Stubborn resolve would allow them to resist breaking said text's commandments.<br /> [\u2026]<br /> furthering the touchstone would involve supporting it (i.e. donating money, advertising, sabotaging rivals etc.) , and Stubborn resolve would allow the deviant fo resist actions that would hurt the business in some way (i.e. revealing secret recipes, giving the owners bad advice, supporting a rival business etc.).<br /> [\u2026]<br /> supporting the touchstone would involve helping the students and/or teachers in some way (promoting the dojo, helping with teaching the students, sabotaging rival dojos), and stubborn resolve would allow the deviant to resist betraying the dojo.<br /> \u200b[\u2026]<br /> supporting the touchstone would involve making sure the con artists prosper and aren't caught, and stubborn resolve would allow them to resist doing anything that would expose expose them or put them out of business. </div> </div> </div>I'm going to assume from the examples that these are supposed to be Loyalty Touchstones for Renegades, in which case &quot;risking danger or suffering for&quot; a Loyalty Touchstone or spending a scene deepening one's relationship is still the standard for healing Stability through the Touchstone; &quot;performing some service for&quot; the Loyalty Touchstone is likewise still the standard for Devoted, which is as correspondingly broad as Renegades' definition of being &quot;in pursuit of&quot; a Conviction Touchstone.<br /> <br /> There is no need to mess around with examples of what Stubborn Resolve helps with, because Stubborn Resolve's applicability requires that you are acting in support of the drives of a Touchstone and trying to avoid being persuaded or compelled away from acting on that drive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T16:45:15-07:00","id":1514639,"title":"","content":"Can a Deviant have a loyalty touchstone that they don't care about as people, but value for personal/selfish reasons? Some examples of what I mean:<br /> 1: A parent Deviant who views their children as extensions of themselves rather than individuals.<br /> 2: A misogynistic Deviant who views his wife/wives as a broodmare(s), a punching bag(s), a sex toy(s) etc.<br /> 3: A slave owning Deviant who views certain slaves as more important than others.<br /> 4: A bully Deviant who enjoys bullying certain people more than others.<br /> 5: A troll Deviant who likes annoying certain people more than others.<br /> 6: A high ranking Devoted who uses the lower ranking Conspiracy members as stress toys via power harassment, sexual harassment, workplace bullying etc.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T17:09:19-07:00","id":1514641,"title":"","content":"If you have a storyteller willing to accept such a Deviant and the other players are comfortable playing with both such a character and such a person as who wants to play such a character then you can. If your storyteller or other players say no, and I certainly wouldn't blame them if they did, then you cannot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T22:15:41-07:00","id":1514650,"title":"","content":"If the question is 'can a Deviant have Loyalty touchstones with whom she has a dysfunctional relationship' then the answer is yes, absolutely. In fact, most such relationships probably are, because it's hard to have a functional relationship when one of the parties involved has a broken soul.<br /> <br /> What you've actually described here, though, is well past that, and most of these are 100% in Conviction Touchstone territory, imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T00:23:03-07:00","id":1514657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1514650#post1514650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the question is 'can a Deviant have Loyalty touchstones with whom she has a dysfunctional relationship' then the answer is yes, absolutely. In fact, most such relationships probably are, because it's hard to have a functional relationship when one of the parties involved has a broken soul.<br /> <br /> What you've actually described here, though, is well past that, and most of these are 100% in Conviction Touchstone territory, imo.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd have to disagree on that last part, deviants want to KILL their conviction touchstones not enslave, exploit, or abuse them. Now the people being abused might have the abuser as their conviction touchstone. What I am describing is more or less Loyalty touchstones that are treated and viewed more like possessions than people; there are men in real life who think women are just fleshlights and incubators, parents in real life who think their kids are just extentions of themselves, slavers in real life who see their slaves as tools etc. To me, it wouldn't seem unrealistic that some especially evil deviants would view their Loyalty touchstones as a favorite tool. A predatory deviant might favor certain &quot;prey&quot; over others, a bully deviant might prefer bullying certain victims over others, a Devoted might bully certain subordinates more than others etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T05:19:12-07:00","id":1514681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1514657#post1514657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd have to disagree on that last part, deviants want to KILL their conviction touchstones not enslave, exploit, or abuse them. Now the people being abused might have the abuser as their conviction touchstone. What I am describing is more or less Loyalty touchstones that are treated and viewed more like possessions than people; there are men in real life who think women are just fleshlights and incubators, parents in real life who think their kids are just extentions of themselves, slavers in real life who see their slaves as tools etc. To me, it wouldn't seem unrealistic that some especially evil deviants would view their Loyalty touchstones as a favorite tool. A predatory deviant might favor certain &quot;prey&quot; over others, a bully deviant might prefer bullying certain victims over others, a Devoted might bully certain subordinates more than others etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Loyalty Touchstone is someone who the deviant's Stability benefits from protecting and/or serving, and who is better able to persuade the deviant to act in ways they suggest. A Touchstone relationship connects a deviant to their former humanity, and Faltering affects both sides of the relationship when it happens.<br /> <br /> It's pretty hard to frame that kind of relationship honestly as &quot;the deviant doesn't think of this person as a person and/or only wants to torment them.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T12:08:39-07:00","id":1514729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1514657#post1514657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd have to disagree on that last part, deviants want to KILL their conviction touchstones not enslave, exploit, or abuse them. Now the people being abused might have the abuser as their conviction touchstone. What I am describing is more or less Loyalty touchstones that are treated and viewed more like possessions than people; there are men in real life who think women are just fleshlights and incubators, parents in real life who think their kids are just extentions of themselves, slavers in real life who see their slaves as tools etc. To me, it wouldn't seem unrealistic that some especially evil deviants would view their Loyalty touchstones as a favorite tool. A predatory deviant might favor certain &quot;prey&quot; over others, a bully deviant might prefer bullying certain victims over others, a Devoted might bully certain subordinates more than others etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Deviants are incentivized in multiple ways to draw out that antagonism instead of blindly going for the kill, not least of which by the way that Conviction touchstones are affirmed in the first place. Killing is the quick hit - an ongoing hostile relationship has better returns over the long run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T07:15:38-07:00","id":1515664,"title":"","content":"The fourth magnitude of the Sensor Array variations allows a Deviant to observe occult phenomena. Can this variation be used to see through illusions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T18:54:53-07:00","id":1515709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1515664#post1515664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fourth magnitude of the Sensor Array variations allows a Deviant to observe occult phenomena. Can this variation be used to see through illusions?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sensor Array</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">She must be aware of the existence of the phenomena she is attempting to observe or protect herself against.\u200b Most people know that fingerprints can be used in an investigation, for example, but someone who doesn\u2019t know that animistic spirits exist cannot easily guess how she must calibrate her senses to see them.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>So, for example, if you wanted to see the fae mien of a changeling, Sensor Array 4 could do that, but only if you already suspect that the changeling has some kind of true visage hidden beneath an illusory Mask.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T21:39:29-07:00","id":1516182,"title":"","content":"If I make a character with multiple powers/variations do they have to have a scar for each one or can my character have just one scar?<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve been playing with this idea of a character that\u2019s like Professor X meets Mystique \u2014 mind reading/control &amp; shapeshifting w/ vocal mimicry. So I think that\u2019d be 4 variations. Anyway for scar I like the idea that whenever the character shapeshifts into someone else the voice of their &quot;victim&quot; (for lack of any other word) becomes a part of the character\u2019s conscious voice. The more they use their powers in a day\u2019s time the more intrusive &amp; darker the &quot;victims&quot; voice/s get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27935-trynmybest","name":"trynmybest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27935_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T21:57:16-07:00","id":1516183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>trynmybest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1516182#post1516182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I make a character with multiple powers/variations do they have to have a scar for each one or can my character have just one scar?</div> </div> </div> </div>Variations the character has, with the exception of the free dot from their Origin, must be entangled with a Scar. A single Scar can only support Variations whose maximum Magnitude and number of additional Variations totals to the Scar's own Magnitude. Anything more will need another Scar or the support of a conspiracy Icon.<br /> <br /> Vocal mimicry is part of the things Face Thief allows you to do starting at Magnitude 2; depending on your criteria for &quot;mind reading/control,&quot; one or more of the core Cephalist Variations should suffice at less than maximum Magnitude, which might allow the whole package to fit onto a single Scar depending on how many Variations and how high their Magnitude is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T00:16:40-07:00","id":1516184,"title":"","content":"Or to put the multiple Variations rule another way:<br /> A five-dot Scar can be entangled with one five-dot Variation, or two four-dot Variations, or three three-dot Variations, or four two-dot Variations, or five one-dot Variations.<br /> A four-dot Scar can be entangled with one four-dot Variation, or two three-dot Variations, or three two-dot Variations, etc.<br /> <br /> This is excluding the one Scar-free Variation dot you receive at chargen. That can be used to give one Variation a Magnitude one dot larger than the Scar it's entangled with could support.<br /> <br /> So, if you wanted to entangle four Variations with a single Scar, one of the four Variations could be a maximum of three dots if it used that scar-free dot, but none of the others could exceed two dots, and that would still take a big old debilitating five-dot Scar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T09:02:20-07:00","id":1518249,"title":"","content":"How could I design a deviant who can only consume specific types of food? Some examples of what I mean;<br /> <br /> 1: A carnivore deviant who can only consume meat<br /> 2: An herbivore deviant who can only consume plant matter<br /> 3: An half-alien deviant who eats metal and is incapable of eating ordinary food.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T11:55:48-07:00","id":1518262,"title":"","content":"The Dependency or Bane Scars, maybe? Or just say that's what it requires, without a mechanical penalty/bonus","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T14:53:53-07:00","id":1518269,"title":"","content":"Maybe create a Form to represent it: think of some minor benefit that goes along with the restricted diet, package them together, and voila!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T18:42:21-07:00","id":1518282,"title":"","content":"1: Can a shapeshifter or illusionist use the exploit the trusting scar by disguising themselves or creating an illusion of one of the deviant's loyalty touchstones? <br /> <br /> 2: Can a deviant with the supersoldier form be tricked into using their loyalty touchstone variations on behalf of an enemy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T12:14:54-07:00","id":1518319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1518249#post1518249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How could I design a deviant who can only consume specific types of food? Some examples of what I mean;<br /> <br /> 1: A carnivore deviant who can only consume meat<br /> 2: An herbivore deviant who can only consume plant matter<br /> 3: An half-alien deviant who eats metal and is incapable of eating ordinary food.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dependency, to be physically able to eat other foods but not draw the needed sustenance from it. Or Bane, to be physically unable to eat other foods. For the alien, entangle with the Inhuman Digestion Variation.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1518282#post1518282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1: Can a shapeshifter or illusionist use the exploit the trusting scar by disguising themselves or creating an illusion of one of the deviant's loyalty touchstones?<br /> <br /> 2: Can a deviant with the supersoldier form be tricked into using their loyalty touchstone variations on behalf of an enemy?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. I might allow this to happen, it's a judgment call. It'd be kind of a jerk Storyteller move to do it all the time. Certainly if the character then found out it was not actually their Touchstone then they would no longer be under the Scar's obligations.<br /> 2. Again, the Variation doesn't magically know if the user is being deceived, it's just based on if the character honestly in good faith thinks they're supporting their Touchstone. Again, this would be kind of a jerk move for the Storyteller to deliberately pull more than once or twice, especially since it's sapping resources the player invested in having.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T14:11:26-07:00","id":1518378,"title":"","content":"Questions about animal transformation:<br /> <br /> 1: Can deviants transform into prehistoric animals like dinosaurs?<br /> 2: If the deviant transforms into a poisonous/venomous animal/swarm like scorpions, snakes, certain species of spiders, etc, can the deviant poison people?<br /> 3: Can a deviant reproduce with normal animals of a species its shapeshifted into? If yes, can the resultant offspring be manticores?<br /> 4: Can a deviants communicate with animals of the same species its transformed into?<br /> 5: Do deviants gain the same weaknesses/limitations of the animals it becomes while transformed? Some examples would be, insect deviants become harmed by bug spray, dog deviants being sickened by chocolate, or fish deviants not being able to breath outside of water.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T22:31:11-07:00","id":1518610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1518378#post1518378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Questions about animal transformation:<br /> <br /> 1: Can deviants transform into prehistoric animals like dinosaurs?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing saying you can't if your ST allows it. You'd still be limited by the Size restrictions, however, which would narrow possible species dramatically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1518378#post1518378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Questions about animal transformation:<br /> <br /> 2: If the deviant transforms into a poisonous/venomous animal/swarm like scorpions, snakes, certain species of spiders, etc, can the deviant poison people?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> \u200b<br /> The rule for the Variation says you are able to attack in any way the animal can. If the animal is venomous, it basically has an attack that can inflict the Poisoned Tilt, possibly Severe depending which animal.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1518378#post1518378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Questions about animal transformation:<br /> <br /> 3: Can a deviant reproduce with normal animals of a species its shapeshifted into? If yes, can the resultant offspring be manticores?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> The book does not address this and would be up to your ST to decide what happens. I would highly advise checking everyone's boundaries before bringing this subject to the table, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1518378#post1518378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Questions about animal transformation:<br /> <br /> 4: Can a deviants communicate with animals of the same species its transformed into?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> Up to the ST, though wouldn't be unreasonable. Voice of the Wild Merit and Pheromones Variation ensure that there wouldn't be a communication barrier ever, however.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1518378#post1518378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Questions about animal transformation:<br /> <br /> 5: Do deviants gain the same weaknesses/limitations of the animals it becomes while transformed? Some examples would be, insect deviants become harmed by bug spray, dog deviants being sickened by chocolate, or fish deviants not being able to breath outside of water.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> You gain the same physical stats including Size and Health of the animal you transform into. The book doesn't address whether you take on the animal's weaknesses despite specifying other things, so you probably don't (outside the things that you would by mechanics). Keep in mind that Humans can also be harmed by bug spray, they just aren't typically around enough quantities of it to seriously affect them, whereas ants are several magnitudes smaller in addition to being so different biologically. You could probably still treat bug spray as a poison, but might be able to get away with chocolate. The fish out of water will probably have a bad time for the few moments until the Deviant remembers to just switch out of animal form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer/Artist | Working on a Deviant: the Renegades story podcast &quot;Gather Round the Trashfires&quot; releasing Feb 2024 | Multiple Deviant STV projects in the queue | Also a Trinity Continuum: Aberrant Storypath Nexus WIP | See my body of work and support me at <a href=\"http://linktr.ee/bekandrew\" target=\"_blank\">linktr.ee/bekandrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28018-bekandrew","name":"bekandrew","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28018_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T14:37:13-07:00","id":1519667,"title":"","content":"For \u201cSkill Specialties\u201d, could you have something like \u201cBrawl (Lash)\u201d? Could you have your Lash as your specialty?<br /> <br /> for Electrokinesis. <b>Conductivity</b> allows you to deal damage up to twice your scar power, but it depends on the power source nearby. If I combine that with <b>Power</b> which allows the Broken to feed/starve electronics. It implies they can <i>create</i> energy. My question is: could they use Power as the energy source for a Conductivity \u2018zap\u2019, or would the energy need to pass into a storage container first? Like a battery of some kind? Like one turn, charge their battery, next turn zap them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28143,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28143-firestar001","user":"firestar001","date":". 08-03-2023, 05:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28143-firestar001","name":"firestar001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T19:35:52-07:00","id":1519699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>firestar001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1519667#post1519667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For \u201cSkill Specialties\u201d, could you have something like \u201cBrawl (Lash)\u201d? Could you have your Lash as your specialty?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Vampire has had its ritual Disciplines listed on the example Specialties for the Skills those forms of blood sorcery use for some time now, and &quot;the Overt supernatural power that gives me a novel form of attack&quot; is sufficiently narrow that it isn't functionally an extra dot for every conceivable use of the Skill.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> for Electrokinesis. <b>Conductivity</b> allows you to deal damage up to twice your scar power, but it depends on the power source nearby. If I combine that with <b>Power</b> which allows the Broken to feed/starve electronics. It implies they can <i>create</i> energy. My question is: could they use Power as the energy source for a Conductivity \u2018zap\u2019, or would the energy need to pass into a storage container first? Like a battery of some kind? Like one turn, charge their battery, next turn zap them. </div> </div> </div>The currently published power for generating an electrical current with a damage rating as described in the Sources of Harm section of the general rules is the Battery Deviation of Integrate Technology. Meanwhile, if you just want a damaging power skinned as an electrical attack, you can use a Lash with the appropriate description.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T14:07:21-07:00","id":1519785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1519699#post1519699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The currently published power for generating an electrical current with a damage rating as described in the Sources of Harm section of the general rules is the Battery Deviation of Integrate Technology. Meanwhile, if you just want a damaging power skinned as an electrical attack, you can use a Lash with the appropriate description.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book, under examples of melee lashes, says: <i>The Invasive has an electrified sword for an arm (Cutting Weaponry Lash; Channel [Electrokinesis], Devastating).</i><br /> <br /> my idea is to make like a lash that is basically a whip stun baton thing. (Deterioration: Arm Wrack and Painful makes it hurt when the tendril emerges from the arm)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28143-firestar001","name":"firestar001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T17:44:52-07:00","id":1519813,"title":"","content":"[nothing to see here; sorry]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":".  Posted in wrong forum 08-04-2023, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T18:31:22-07:00","id":1519816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1519813#post1519813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, you might consider <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>'s closest counterpart to the Nephandi, namely the Scelesti. The discussion there about Antinomianism is definitely relevant; and the sections about befouling and otherwise inverting Magic, while increasingly tied to <b>Awakening</b>'s notion of Watchtowers, can still be mined for ideas about why a Nephandus might choose to invest their Avatar or corrupt their Focus.<br /> <br /> And speaking of that: you might want to look at <b>Prism of Focus</b>, on Storyteller's Vault. It's not particularly about the Nephandi; it's primarily about making Practices clearer and more useful. But it has a section about Corrupted Practices which might be worth a look.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this wound up in the wrong place, this is the ask a question thread in Deviant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T19:12:08-07:00","id":1519818,"title":"","content":"Thanks; I don't know how that happened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T19:24:33-07:00","id":1519820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>firestar001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1519785#post1519785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book, under examples of melee lashes, says: <i>The Invasive has an electrified sword for an arm (Cutting Weaponry Lash; Channel [Electrokinesis], Devastating).</i><br /> <br /> my idea is to make like a lash that is basically a whip stun baton thing. (Deterioration: Arm Wrack and Painful makes it hurt when the tendril emerges from the arm)</div> </div> </div> </div>The example means means that the deviant has a Lash that can also use the effects of Electrokinesis through a successful attack instead of a Scar Finesse roll. If it just does damage and/or inflicts Tilts you build an appropriate Lash and be done with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T08:38:32-07:00","id":1519867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>firestar001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1519785#post1519785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">my idea is to make like a lash that is basically a whip stun baton thing. (Deterioration: Arm Wrack and Painful makes it hurt when the tendril emerges from the arm)</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's all you want, making it a Lash with the Disabling/Debilitating effect/Deviation and/or the Stunning Deviation is much simpler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-05T12:05:22-07:00","id":1522113,"title":"","content":"Hello!<br /> My question is: you can get deviations for Variations and Scars for free or they have a cost?<br /> <br /> Also, they're optional?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-05T15:02:03-07:00","id":1522121,"title":"","content":"Deviations have a \u201ccost\u201d, in that they adjust the balance between the Variation and the entangled Scar: a +1 Deviation on a Variation, for example, requires you to entangle the Variation with a Scar one level higher than it would normally need to be entangled with. And yes, they're optional: they exist to refine what the Variation does, letting a single Variation cover a wider range of concepts than might be at first supposed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-19T15:12:44-07:00","id":1522801,"title":"","content":"How do I create a deviant who requires large amounts of sleep?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-19T18:58:15-07:00","id":1522811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1522801#post1522801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> How do I create a deviant who requires large amounts of sleep?</div> </div> </div> </div>Genetic Disorder 3 and other sources of the Fatigued Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-11T19:25:28-07:00","id":1523985,"title":"","content":"Apologies if this has already been mentioned elsewhere, but I have been unable to find any online tools to randomize the creation of a remade as per Launch Devoted Line on page 29 of The Devoted Companion. <br /> <br /> If no tools exist, what is the consensus on how they should be randomized? Scars or variations first? How should variations be generated to ensure that half or more of its variations are from universal/clade-it-belongs-to? At what point do you add the scar-free variation from its origin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28213-raw_brewer_devoted","name":"RAW_brewer_devoted","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28213_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-11T21:08:15-07:00","id":1523988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RAW_brewer_devoted</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1523985#post1523985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If no tools exist, what is the consensus on how they should be randomized? Scars or variations first? How should variations be generated to ensure that half or more of its variations are from universal/clade-it-belongs-to? At what point do you add the scar-free variation from its origin?</div> </div> </div> </div>The way Divergences work mean there isn't really a practical way to randomize its results without involving some sort of large language model to identify when e.g. Pyrokinesis is not an appropriate Variation to arise from an experimental cryogenics procedure. As the sidebar on the preceding page says, the point is more for there to be inherent uncertainty in dabbling with the Divergence \u2014 as a player-facing tool, Launch Devoted Line dedicates an exceptional success effect to guaranteeing some of the results are the specific things you were trying for to emphasize that uncertainty, but the outcome otherwise is as much in the Storyteller's hands as whether Recruit Devoted turns out a deep-cover spy or a press-ganged Renegade or a far-gone Feral.<br /> <br /> As far as generalizable notes, the following Universal Variations tend to be broadly applicable: Brachiation, Carapace, Enhanced Speed, Hyper-Competence, Immunity, Lash, Specialized Sense, and Superhuman (Attribute). Flashier and more esoteric fare will likely depend on the method of Divergence, which in turn will probably suggest an appropriate Clade and to a lesser extent the probable Origin. Following the standard character creation order of picking Variations and then picking Scars to counterbalance them is probably the best bet unless you have a Scar in mind from the jump.<br /> <br /> The fact that Projects are attached to Nodes responsible for ensuring they come to fruition and Launch Devoted Line specifically requires an appropriate Node for the task should lend some ideas about how the conspiracy is attempting to produce a Divergence just as surely as its Principles and Anchors would inform its reasons for doing so and/or what might complicate it. Like most supernatural beings with character full sheets, the Remade aren't really narratively suited to serving throwaway roles for which a true randomizer would be appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-24T07:04:57-07:00","id":1524475,"title":"","content":"How do I create a Lash that has the effect of lowering a person's body temperature?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-24T09:10:01-07:00","id":1524478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1524475#post1524475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do I create a Lash that has the effect of lowering a person's body temperature?</div> </div> </div> </div>Have it apply the Tilt that produces the mechanical effect you are trying to produce by doing so, or skin it as doing so if you do not need it to have a mechanical effect (possibly applying the Identifier Deviation if you want this to be a distinguishing feature).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-23T16:16:26-08:00","id":1525867,"title":"","content":"Rapid Healing + Bane??<br /> <br /> Making a phoenix-like character. Bane is gonna be something like cold or water (maybe water of a certain temperature idk). Level 2 says you can't heal damage by any means. But Rapid Healing lets you heal damage. And Bane does NOT cancel out Rapid Healing so....<br /> <br /> Could/Would Bane just negate natural healing, but allow other healing to happen? (Like from a Demon's embed)<br /> Would the end result be a constant 1 damage done to the hit point box? Or depending on the severity of the damage, 1 less point?<br /> <br /> <br /> I mean I KNOW doing Rapid Healing + Power Failure might be better. But I'm looking to get the question answered mainly because I'm curious about this little paradox. <br /> <br /> Personally I'm leaning on the thought of just taking one damage after the one heal. Thus giving the player a constant 1 point of bashing or lethal damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28143-firestar001","name":"firestar001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-23T16:50:02-08:00","id":1525868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>firestar001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1525867#post1525867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rapid Healing + Bane??<br /> <br /> Making a phoenix-like character. Bane is gonna be something like cold or water (maybe water of a certain temperature idk). Level 2 says you can't heal damage by any means. But Rapid Healing lets you heal damage. And Bane does NOT cancel out Rapid Healing so....</div> </div> </div> </div>Rapid Healing explicitly doesn't work on damage caused by Scars. Bane is a Scar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could/Would Bane just negate natural healing, but allow other healing to happen? (Like from a Demon's embed) </div> </div> </div>&quot;By any means&quot; means <i>by any means.</i> While the character is touching or otherwise directly exposed to the Bane, they can't heal. Period.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean I KNOW doing Rapid Healing + Power Failure might be better. But I'm looking to get the question answered mainly because I'm curious about this little paradox. </div> </div> </div>Rapid Healing + Power Failure wouldn't work because of the specific requirement that Rapid Healing be a Persistent Perpetual Variation \u2014 Power Failure is a Controlled Scar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-23-2023, 07:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-23T18:54:17-08:00","id":1525872,"title":"","content":"Perhaps <b><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28143-firestar001\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">firestar001</span></a></b> would be interested in Rapid Healing + Hemophilia? Or Rapid Healing + Thin Skin?<br /> <br /> As the 5 dot version of Rapid Healing means that you don't need to worry about dying from extra damage or fewer health boxes.<br /> <br /> There is also the Philia scar from the Devoted Companion, although you just have to ne careful not to take the lethal damage bullet point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28213,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28213-raw_brewer_devoted","user":"RAW_brewer_devoted","date":". 11-23-2023, 10:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28213-raw_brewer_devoted","name":"RAW_brewer_devoted","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28213_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-23T19:26:06-08:00","id":1525873,"title":"","content":"To the person that asked about rapid healing plus bane. Watch the old TV series Carivale. Certain characters had healing powers that drained life from any living thing near the person being healed. <br /> <br /> It strikes me that you could have a PC whose Rapid Healing drained life force from any living thing near them uncontrollably. Thus making them an involuntary vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-24T11:52:06-08:00","id":1525882,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ll admit I totally forgot about the whole \u201ccan\u2019t heal damage from scars\u201d. Sorry for sounding stupid all. ^^;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28143-firestar001","name":"firestar001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-27T20:12:14-08:00","id":1526032,"title":"","content":"Potentially a dumb question<br /> <br /> can a Lash &quot;Channel&quot; a Lash? For instance if I had 2 \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Variations attached to a \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Power Failure Scar, where<br /> <br /> Variation [a] is a ranged cutting Channel (Channeling Variation [b]) Lash with the &quot;Explosive&quot; and &quot;Line-of-Sight&quot; deviations<br /> <br /> Variation [b] is a ranged cutting Channel (Channeling Variation [a]) Lash with the &quot;Explosive&quot; and &quot;Incinerating&quot; deviations<br /> <br /> If the Story Teller allowed for the Megumin build, would it, upon activation, ping pong between Variation [a] and [b] until all targets in the initial blast radius had either died or received less than lethal damage? Or would it spread beyond the initial explosion radius if valid targets were lethally damaged in subsequent explosions? Or did I misread it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28213-raw_brewer_devoted","name":"RAW_brewer_devoted","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28213_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-27T20:54:32-08:00","id":1526035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RAW_brewer_devoted</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1526032#post1526032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Potentially a dumb question<br /> <br /> can a Lash &quot;Channel&quot; a Lash? For instance if I had 2 \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Variations attached to a \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Power Failure Scar, where<br /> <br /> Variation [a] is a ranged cutting Channel (Channeling Variation [b]) Lash with the &quot;Explosive&quot; and &quot;Line-of-Sight&quot; deviations<br /> <br /> Variation [b] is a ranged cutting Channel (Channeling Variation [a]) Lash with the &quot;Explosive&quot; and &quot;Incinerating&quot; deviations<br /> <br /> If the Story Teller allowed for the Megumin build, would it, upon activation, ping pong between Variation [a] and [b] until all targets in the initial blast radius had either died or received less than lethal damage? Or would it spread beyond the initial explosion radius if valid targets were lethally damaged in subsequent explosions? Or did I misread it?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a general rule if you read something and think &quot;wow, this single thing can defeat everything, ever, with no roll&quot; odds are the answer is no, it doesn't work like that. Even if the RAW did, no storyteller would or should allow it. <br /> <br /> As to your specific instance, no, it doesn't work. Channel only works on directed variations. Lash does not qualify.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-27T21:43:48-08:00","id":1526037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RAW_brewer_devoted</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1526032#post1526032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Potentially a dumb question<br /> <br /> can a Lash &quot;Channel&quot; a Lash? For instance if I had 2 \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Variations attached to a \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Power Failure Scar, where<br /> <br /> Variation [a] is a ranged cutting Channel (Channeling Variation [b]) Lash with the &quot;Explosive&quot; and &quot;Line-of-Sight&quot; deviations<br /> <br /> Variation [b] is a ranged cutting Channel (Channeling Variation [a]) Lash with the &quot;Explosive&quot; and &quot;Incinerating&quot; deviations<br /> <br /> If the Story Teller allowed for the Megumin build, would it, upon activation, ping pong between Variation [a] and [b] until all targets in the initial blast radius had either died or received less than lethal damage? Or would it spread beyond the initial explosion radius if valid targets were lethally damaged in subsequent explosions? Or did I misread it?</div> </div> </div> </div>As Shadowcat says, despite the exceptions for entangling Scars and Deviations, a Lash is not a Directed Variation and so cannot be Channeled \u2014 ranged Lashes can have drawbacks akin to those the system uses with other forms of ranged targeted effect, but the thing that the Variation &quot;Lash&quot; <i>does</i> is give you a new form of attack rather than serve as the attack itself.<br /> <br /> More stylistically, when the game disallows nesting Secondary Scars, it seems self-evident that recursive nested Variations are beyond the bounds of reason to permit and the system does not presently contain generic rules for stacking explosions having any effect on their blast radius.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-02T20:56:46-08:00","id":1526263,"title":"","content":"Some Node-based questions after reading the Devoted Companion again:<br /> <br /> Does a Privileges-type Organizational Icon functioning &quot;almost exactly like a Privilege&quot; include its inability to be moved to another Node?<br /> <br /> Is an &quot;abandoned Node&quot; just a Node formerly belonging to a conspiracy that has been destroyed, and/or can a Node that has been used in an Expel- or Reform-type purge be assimilated with a Complexity 1 Project as well?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 12-03-2023, 12:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-03T06:51:57-08:00","id":1526276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1526263#post1526263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some Node-based questions after reading the Devoted Companion again:<br /> <br /> Does a Privileges-type Organizational Icon functioning &quot;almost exactly like a Privilege&quot; include its inability to be moved to another Node?</div> </div> </div> </div>That wasn't my intent, but the entry implies it (the danger of using the space-saving &quot;works the same as X&quot; language, I suppose). If you want to allow Privilege Icons to be moved to another Node, I'd say it's the table's call to make.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1526263#post1526263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is an &quot;abandoned Node&quot; just a Node formerly belonging to a conspiracy that has been destroyed, and/or can a Node that has been used in an Expel- or Reform-type purge be assimilated with a Complexity 1 Project as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>The language here is a bit vague (sorry about that). The narrative goal is for a conspiracy to be able to find resources another conspiracy has abandoned or lost and assimilate them into itself. This can be a Node that has been purged or one destroyed due to the loss of its Linchpin. In some cases, it would even be appropriate to allow a conspiracy to assimilate one that was blown up, burned down, buried under rubble, sent to the bottom of the sea, etc., as the inspirational media often includes examples of an organization finding something powerful and dangerous in the ruins of a defunct organization. It shouldn't be used as a way to cheat by purging a Node to clear a bunch of damage to Association and then immediately spending a single Effort to assimilate the Node again a chapter later.<br /> <br /> The upside is that this kind of Project is cheap. The man downside is that the conspiracy has no control over the nature of the Node it is assimilating; beggars can't be choosers (unless the conspiracy takes out a rival's Linchpin and then quickly assimilates the Node she led).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-28T05:30:06-08:00","id":1527546,"title":"","content":"I got an idea for a name for the Deviant \u201cNight Horrors\u201d book. \u201cNight Horrors: Blacksite Projects\u201d<br /> <br /> eh? Eh? (Sorry. Came to me at work and wanted to share it)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28143-firestar001","name":"firestar001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T19:45:21-08:00","id":1530602,"title":"","content":"When will the Clade Deviant book be release?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T19:57:03-08:00","id":1530603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1530602#post1530602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When will the Clade Deviant book be release?</div> </div> </div> </div>At last check in the February 5th Monday Meeting notes, it's in Layout. No additional notes since January 2, but it moved to that step in September 2023. For partial context, The Hedge moved to Layout from Art Direction at the start of this year. For further context, there is no set timetable for these steps because every book is different and things can happen to throw off the schedule.<br /> <br /> Presumably some time this year, given that it's a KS stretch goal and one of the two other remaining steps is done after errata collection with advance copies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-28T10:27:27-07:00","id":1534852,"title":"","content":"Making sure I'm reading the mixed-branch effects of the Preparation Scar correctly:<br /> <br /> 1. The Magnitude 4 &quot;Balanced&quot; effect requires the deviant to perform a ritual that deprives them of their Defense for a number of turns determined by Scar Resistance, which happens before rolling; in addition, once the ritual is done, the roll to activate the Variation is an extended action with a fixed interval length and a target number equal to twice the Variation's Magnitude. Therefore, a deviant with Scar Resistance 3 attempting to activate a Magnitude 4 Variation entangled with Balanced Preparation would take two turns/fifteen minutes to prepare and however many turns/singular minutes it takes them to accumulate eight successes on the Scar Finesse roll, rather than one or the other, though they would only lose their Defense for those first two turns/fifteen minutes.<br /> <br /> 2. The Magnitude 5 effect works as above, except the extended action also deprives the deviant of their Defense, the interval on the extended action is also fifteen minutes, and the deviant can't prepare the Variation in the context of an action scene, so the amount of time it would take to activate the same Magnitude 4 Variation would jump to fifteen minutes multiplied by [1+ number of rolls to achieve eight successes].<br /> <br /> Do I have that right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-28T17:10:32-07:00","id":1534868,"title":"","content":"That all scans right to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https