ass=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1539561#post1539561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If an Outsider has Hypercompetence or Computer Aided Processessing, do the variations negate the extra penalties an outsider suffers from untrained social skills?</div> </div> </div> </div>Computer-Aided Processing has nothing to do with unSkilled penalties and Hyper-Competence doesn't actually give you Skill dots. As with similar interactions with the Frozen Heart Scars, whether Omnicompetence 1's &quot;no untrained Skill penalties&quot; effect supercedes an effect that specifically increases those penalties is up to your table, though the penalty to rolls to make a first impression still applies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T03:10:22-07:00","id":1539836,"title":"","content":"Question: if I put my free scar dot on a 2 dots Variation, I still can bound it to a 2 dots scar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T04:44:32-07:00","id":1539843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1539836#post1539836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: if I put my free scar dot on a 2 dots Variation, I still can bound it to a 2 dots scar?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Only Variation Magnitude that is not Scar-free is used when comparing it to the Magnitude of a Scar for the purposes of seeing if the Scar is severe enough to entangle that Variation along with any others. If you have a Magnitude 3 Scar, you could entangle it with two Magnitude 2 Variations and put your Scar-free dot of Variation Magnitude on one of them to have that Scar entangled with a Magnitude 3 and Magnitude 2 Variation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T04:55:38-07:00","id":1539844,"title":"","content":"So if I put my free dot on a magnitude 1 lash, it becomes a magnitude 2 lash, and yet I can entangle it to a magitude 1 scar. I'm right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T05:18:02-07:00","id":1539846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1539844#post1539844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if I put my free dot on a magnitude 1 lash, it becomes a magnitude 2 lash, and yet I can entangle it to a magitude 1 scar. I'm right?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's correct. Another option is to use it for a Magnitude 1 Variation that isn't entangled with a Scar at all (choosing whether it uses your Mental, Physical, or Social Attributes for Scar Power/Finesse/Resistance).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-20T07:10:38-07:00","id":1540765,"title":"","content":"What scars could I use to reflect a reptile deviant's cold-bloodedness?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-20T07:27:18-07:00","id":1540766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1540765#post1540765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What scars could I use to reflect a reptile deviant's cold-bloodedness?</div> </div> </div> </div>Native Environment or Frozen Heart, depending on which sort of &quot;cold-blooded&quot; you're aiming for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-24T11:51:29-07:00","id":1540966,"title":"","content":"Question, how many Variations/Threat Level, would a Deviant have to be on par with other starting characters for a multi-splat game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25650-jacook03","name":"Jacook03","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25650_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-24T14:52:08-07:00","id":1540973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacook03</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1540966#post1540966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question, how many Variations/Threat Level, would a Deviant have to be on par with other starting characters for a multi-splat game?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really something that has a concrete answer, because the gamelines aren't made for parity and for the most part a Deviant's Variations are all the supernatural benefits they get from their template and those can run the gamut of equivalence from &quot;this is a Favored Attribute with room to grow&quot; to &quot;this is accelerated healing the likes of which werewolves have to be trying to kill something to tap into&quot; to &quot;this is a flashy supernatural power akin to a Royal Contract or an Exploit.&quot; The need to balance Variation Magnitude with Scars coupled with the breadth of modularity for Variations and Scars and the ability to have Scar-free Magnitude means that comparison is going to frequently come down to the individual level.<br /> <br /> As far as broad strokes, a Threat Level of Dysplasia with your highest Variation at Magnitude 3 puts the character's Supernatural Tolerance at the threshold of where the games tend to balance typical PC supernatural activity \u2014 most of the games broadly assume you've reached the main part of the character's life cycle in the Supernatural Potency 3-5 range.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-24T18:32:28-07:00","id":1540981,"title":"","content":"Thank you, again. You have been most helpful in regards for giving me well thought out answers of late. Much appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25650-jacook03","name":"Jacook03","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25650_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-24T19:44:06-07:00","id":1540983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacook03</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1540966#post1540966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question, how many Variations/Threat Level, would a Deviant have to be on par with other starting characters for a multi-splat game?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've asked that question before myself and never received an answer I was entirely happy with. Part of the problem is what are you trying to balance against, a Mummy or Mage will have a different answer than a Single Sater or Hunter. Generally I would probably say 7 or 8 but no variations above 3 but that's aiming for a vampire / werewolf power level, not a mummy one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T09:15:03-07:00","id":1542116,"title":"","content":"How does the Uplift Form from the Clade Companion intersect with Origins (StreetThane from the fiction is obviously an Exomorph, but how would a Genotypal etc. become Remade?)?<br /> I'm assuming most Uplifts would be Chimerics due to being spliced/stitched/w/e with (parts of) humans/part-human Supernaturals (and you'll want to give them General or Chimeric Variations anyway), but can a f.e. Coactive Uplift be made by shoving a wind spirit into a dog etc.?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T09:49:21-07:00","id":1542117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1542116#post1542116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does the Uplift Form from the Clade Companion intersect with Origins (StreetThane from the fiction is obviously an Exomorph, but how would a Genotypal etc. become Remade?)?<br /> I'm assuming most Uplifts would be Chimerics due to being spliced/stitched/w/e with (parts of) humans/part-human Supernaturals (and you'll want to give them General or Chimeric Variations anyway), but can a f.e. Coactive Uplift be made by shoving a wind spirit into a dog etc.?</div> </div> </div> </div>The key thing to remember with Uplifts is that that Form alone just represents a Deviant with the body of an animal; an Uplift Divergence can be like any other human Divergence except that the end result was the body of a rhinoceros just as easily as it can model the corebook's mention of attempting to make Manticores with too much intelligence producing things more like Deviants.<br /> <br /> Autourgics and Epimorphs who used to be animals are probably thin on the ground, but &quot;I wanted superpowers [for their own sake/to get rich] and turned myself into a giant salamander&quot; is as much a valid Uplift Origin as &quot;we genetically modified these dogs until they produced offspring smart enough to levitate small objects with their minds, and then <i>those</i> children produced a Corgi with sufficient intelligence to reenact <i>Carrie.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> Ditto for Clades; most animals aren't likely to have a theory of mind advanced enough to produce a Cephalist, but a person being so traumatized that you permanently turned into a rat can happen as readily as freak radiation exposure could impart the gift of speech and illusion to an elephant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 09-14-2024, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T12:17:18-07:00","id":1542123,"title":"","content":"An actual mechanics question.<br /> <br /> Does an Uplift use base or adjusted Attributes for 1) derived statistics like Speed, 2) Merit prerequisites? I'm currently assuming it's 1) adjusted 2) base, but a clarification would be helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T09:02:58-07:00","id":1542181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1542123#post1542123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does an Uplift use base or adjusted Attributes for 1) derived statistics like Speed</div> </div> </div> </div>As mundane actions, they'd use the adjusted Attributes. Defense uses the base Attributes for the calculation to check against their species' listed Defense as described in the writeup.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Merit prerequisites? </div> </div> </div>I would take the same tack as described in Superhuman Attribute, i.e. as a modification to the deviant's stats that doesn't go away, it counts. (Omnicompetence's Skill boosts are consistently temporary dots even at the highest Magnitude and thus wouldn't work quite the same).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T10:33:39-07:00","id":1542323,"title":"","content":"What scars could I use to create a deviant that looks human on the surface, but a DNA analysis, x-ray, ultrasound, etc. would show that they are clearly not normal? For example, a deviant that has an inhuman blood type or one with missing internal organs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T11:06:15-07:00","id":1542325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1542323#post1542323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What scars could I use to create a deviant that looks human on the surface, but a DNA analysis, x-ray, ultrasound, etc. would show that they are clearly not normal? For example, a deviant that has an inhuman blood type or one with missing internal organs?</div> </div> </div> </div>You might be able to slant Conspicuous Appearance 1 in that direction, but generally speaking unless those differences have effects other than subsurface/non-visible-spectrum aesthetic tells they aren't Scars.<br /> <br /> You could create a Universal Deviation that runs the gamut of Magnitude modifications, but unless your inhuman blood type has a mechanical effect it's not going to support Variations or substantially impede the deviant's life and/or goals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T13:46:46-07:00","id":1542334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1542323#post1542323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What scars could I use to create a deviant that looks human on the surface, but a DNA analysis, x-ray, ultrasound, etc. would show that they are clearly not normal? For example, a deviant that has an inhuman blood type or one with missing internal organs?</div> </div> </div> </div>What Satchel said, but I'd add that if those changes has some additional effect, they'd much more easily be covered by Scars. Genetic Disorder and Sluggish Metabolism would fit many of these great. Fragility, Hemophilia and Thin Skin could also work well. Dependency/Maintenance could work if you need to compensate for your change. Then just flavour the Scar to be something that an in-depth examination could<br /> <br /> A different (and in my opinion better) way of going about it is to take Anomalous Biology. Sure, it's a Variation and thus primarily a bonus and would require a Scar to entangle it with, but having a Variation can often by itself be a liability. Unlike the Scars I mentioned, you don't even have to flavour it to work as you want. Someone with any of the Bloodless, Heartless, Lifeless and Mindless effects straight up would not register on the relevant medical instruments. The others can also be observed, even if it's much easier to fake them (or, for Ageless, just takes way too long to test).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-26T09:19:58-07:00","id":1542690,"title":"","content":"I want to know what variations and/or scars I could use to produce deviant's with these specific powers/weaknesses.<br /> <br /> 1: I have an idea for a deviant who has a bane scar, but the catch is that their bane has to be injected or ingested and is otherwise harmless. An example of this would be a demon deviant who can touch holy water and is only harmed if they swallow it or has it injected into their system.<br /> <br /> 2: A variant of the Rapid Healing Variation that requires some kind of fuel. An example of this would be a part spirit deviant whose healing factor is fueled by their specific essence or a vampire-like deviant who needs to drink blood to fuel their healing factor.<br /> <br /> 3: A variant of the bane scar where only one specific body parts is affected to the bane. An example of this would be a deviant with the left arm of a vampire whose arm is harmed by sunlight, but the rest of them isn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27678,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","user":"cybirddude","date":". 09-26-2024, 12:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-26T14:52:10-07:00","id":1542716,"title":"","content":"1) Sounds like a -1 Magnitude Deviation.<br /> 2) Dependency (Ill) seems like the obvious one.<br /> 3) Sounds like a -1 Magnitude Deviation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-30T11:42:32-08:00","id":1548062,"title":"","content":"Remind me, can Deviant move variations between scars?<br /> <br /> Example: We have Lash &amp; another Lash + Bane. Deviant got a new scar, can I move my lash here? Should I pay for such action?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-30T12:55:56-08:00","id":1548066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1548062#post1548062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remind me, can Deviant move variations between scars?<br /> <br /> Example: We have Lash &amp; another Lash + Bane. Deviant got a new scar, can I move my lash here? Should I pay for such action?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;If the player feels her character has too many Scars to reasonably play, or if a Scar that seemed interesting at the time<br /> impedes her ability to have fun (or makes it less fun for everyone<br /> in the troupe), the Storyteller may allow her to replace a Scar<br /> with one of equal Magnitude or to fuse two or more Scars<br /> into a single Scar. This must always result in a legal number<br /> of entangled Variations attached to each Scar.&quot;<br /> <br /> Based on this, it seems perfectly reasonable to switch between existing Scars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-16T07:13:22-08:00","id":1548526,"title":"","content":"Can Deviant be Touchstones to one another (including players)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-16T08:51:36-08:00","id":1548530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1548526#post1548526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Deviant be Touchstones to one another (including players)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Concretely, page 62 mentions the prospect of a Feral being one of a Deviant's Loyalty Touchstones, and a common cause of Nemeses is one of the Devoted losing a Loyalty Touchstone and thereby having more reliance on their Conviction Touchstones (who are often Remade targets they have been pointed at by their conspiracy). Marginally less officially, Shallow Graves has a sidebar in its extensive discussion of Touchstones that includes notes about pitfalls to avoid when one has declared a fellow member of the cohort as a Touchstone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-23T04:36:44-08:00","id":1548728,"title":"","content":"Another chaotical idea:<br /> <br /> If Deviant has Outsider form. How to represent spiritual influence over flesh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-23T06:40:49-08:00","id":1548730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1548728#post1548728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another chaotical idea:<br /> <br /> If Deviant has Outsider form. How to represent spiritual influence over flesh?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the type of influence, but Sacred Flesh (and Cursed Flesh from <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves\" target=\"_blank\">Shallow Graves</a>) are broadly useful for giving the effects of Variations and Scars to other people.<br /> <br /> Other Variations that might be apropos to represent influence over flesh (whether your own or other people's) include Aquatic, Boneless, Brachiation, Camouflage, Carapace, Environmental Adaptation, Face Thief, Flight, Gigantic, Healer, Immunity, Miniaturization, Shadow Selves, Specialized Sense (Animal), Superhuman Attribute, Animal Transformation, Mimicry, Monstrous Transformation, Pheromones; if you have Shallow Graves, you might also find Sticky Filaments, Stretching, Extra Appendages, Body Modification, Matter Emulation, and/or Gestalt suitable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-23T10:46:40-08:00","id":1548733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1548730#post1548730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*obvious truth*</div> </div> </div> </div>Angry <a href=\"https://i.imgflip.com/1xgcsn.jpg?a483384\" target=\"_blank\">bird </a>meme<br /> Well, you are right. I just wasn't sure about influencing others, which is still slightly hard for classic Coactive deviants. At least I think Outsiders are coactive.<br /> On the other hand, if body is a vessel maybe Mutant will work too. <hr /><br /> More questions:<br /> <br /> Will Lash specialty apply to Prototype? If it is classic laser Lash.<br /> <br /> Icons: If my conspiracy collects pacts with otherwordly demons and each pact (ritualistic Prototypes) is formed between specific deviant (or their 3D bioprinter) and something on the other side. Will each such pact count as a separate Icon?<br /> <br /> Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","user":"Alphari","date":". 02-23-2025, 02:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-23T12:57:53-08:00","id":1548735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1548733#post1548733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will Lash specialty apply to Prototype? If it is classic laser Lash.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would likely vary from table to table, given that Prototypes are specifically equipment and Lash covers everything from conjured swords and missile hardpoints to venomous claws and tactical beehives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Icons: If my conspiracy collects pacts with otherwordly demons and each pact (ritualistic Prototypes) is formed between specific deviant (or their 3D bioprinter) and something on the other side. Will each such pact count as a separate Icon? </div> </div> </div>Agent Icons can provide their benefits under the limits described in the Devoted Companion, and the need to attach an Icon to a Node will limit the people it works for or at the very least build in a failure mode for any benefits derived from that Icon, but a single Icon can provide arrays of Variations such that, for instance, a Standing 3 conspiracy can give each of a handful of agents of a Node one of three different pre-set packages of 2 Magnitude of Variations with commensurate Scars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-01T05:59:42-08:00","id":1548845,"title":"","content":"Random thought: What if deviant has a supernatural Resolve 3. Yet, some another pesky deviant dropped Cursed Flesh (from SG) with Suppression [Resolve] 3.<ul><li>How will it work? Calculate first resolve then scar? Or opposite?</li> <li>What if Deviant has S Resolve 3, but is targeted by Suppression 2? What about Suppression 4?</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-01T07:00:01-08:00","id":1548846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1548845#post1548845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random thought: What if deviant has a supernatural Resolve 3. Yet, some another pesky deviant dropped Cursed Flesh (from SG) with Suppression [Resolve] 3.<ul><li>How will it work? Calculate first resolve then scar? Or opposite?</li> <li>What if Deviant has S Resolve 3, but is targeted by Suppression 2? What about Suppression 4?</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>As far as basic order of operations goes, I would say the Variation adds to the deviant's Resolve first, then Cursed Flesh subtracts from the increased Resolve, because doing it in the opposite order means the Variation's minimum Attribute effect would cause Suppression that takes the Attribute below the minimum to not have any additional effect.<br /> <br /> For Suppression 2, nothing changes because Suppression doesn't actually affect the rating of an Attribute until Magnitude 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-01T07:11:44-08:00","id":1548847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1548845#post1548845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random thought: What if deviant has a supernatural Resolve 3. Yet, some another pesky deviant dropped Cursed Flesh (from SG) with Suppression [Resolve] 3.<ul><li>How will it work? Calculate first resolve then scar? Or opposite?</li> <li>What if Deviant has S Resolve 3, but is targeted by Suppression 2? What about Suppression 4?</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>First you resolve the effect of Superhuman Resolve 3, i.e. the Clash of Wills for mind-affecting powers.<br /> <br /> Then you calculate your Resolve. +3 from Superhuman Resolve 3 and -1 from Suppression 3. No need to care about the order. X+3-1 equals X-1+3 equals X+2.<br /> <br /> If this puts your Resolve below the limit for Superhuman Resolve 3 (i.e. the minimum is 6), then we have two powers that are in direct conflict with each other:<br /> Resolve this with a Clash of Wills (a regular CoW, so you don't get the ability to reroll once per turn by spending WP as with the Superhuman Resolve special effect).<br /> <br /> If the target wins, their Resolve remains at 6. If the Cursed Flesh-user wins, the target's Resolve is lowered below 6.<br /> <br /> For Suppression 2, just skip everything except the first step (the CoW against mind-affecting powers) since it doesn't lower the attribute rating.<br /> For Suppression 4, it works just like for Suppression 3 except larger Resolve penalty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-11T14:26:05-07:00","id":1549166,"title":"","content":"Random thoughts about Shallow Graves (not sure if it is right place to ask):<br /> <br /> 1) There is Cyclical Scar (3) which shifts magnitude under (un)known factors, similar to Fluctuating Variation in main book. As we build each magnitude of that scar - can players change/rotate DEVIATIONS on each magnitude level?<br /> Example: Glitch 1, Glitch 2, Glitch 2 + Nightmare, Glitch 3 + Suppressible Variation + Caveat, Glitch 5<br /> <br /> 2) Same scar, but now I decreased its magnitude to 2. I want to increase it to Mag 3 by using SG's deviation twined scar (which add scar of same magnitude, but they both count as Mag+1). Should it remain the same during magnitude changes, or should it increase its magnitude if Scar goes above its starting magnitude?<br /> <br /> 3) Can player use Cyclical Scar as twined scar aka We have main scar - Glitch 2, now I add Cyclical Scar (alternative persona) as part of twined scar deviation. Or is it somehow forbidden / illogical move?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-11T18:06:30-07:00","id":1549177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1549166#post1549166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) There is Cyclical Scar (3) which shifts magnitude under (un)known factors, similar to Fluctuating Variation in main book. As we build each magnitude of that scar - can players change/rotate DEVIATIONS on each magnitude level?<br /> Example: Glitch 1, Glitch 2, Glitch 2 + Nightmare, Glitch 3 + Suppressible Variation + Caveat, Glitch 5</div> </div> </div> </div>The verbiage seems to indicate that the details of the Scar's changes in Magnitude are set at each Magnitude, so all instances of the Scar's Magnitude 2/3/4/etc phase work the same whenever it's at that Magnitude.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Same scar, but now I decreased its magnitude to 2. I want to increase it to Mag 3 by using SG's deviation twined scar (which add scar of same magnitude, but they both count as Mag+1). Should it remain the same during magnitude changes, or should it increase its magnitude if Scar goes above its starting magnitude?<br /> <br /> 3) Can player use Cyclical Scar as twined scar aka We have main scar - Glitch 2, now I add Cyclical Scar (alternative persona) as part of twined scar deviation. Or is it somehow forbidden / illogical move? </div> </div> </div>Per the corebook's notes on Nesting Scars (page 111), you cannot choose a Scar that has a Secondary Scar to act as a Secondary Scar itself; Cyclical Scar works by choosing a secondary Scar and therefore cannot be a Twined Scar nor benefit from the Twined Scar Standard Deviation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-22T07:38:35-07:00","id":1550318,"title":"","content":"Can someone explain me custom variations? I am trying to convert DtF Lores into Variations. There are few details in that system, which I don't understand.<ul><li>How should I emulate high Magnitude powers by combining 2 or more lower Mag powers?</li> </ul>I know that Mag3 can be made from 3 Mag1 variations, or 2 Mag2. But if I have Mag2 variations which are made from pairs of Mag1 - it makes things confusing.<ul><li>Or maybe it would be better to ask - &quot;should I calculate each individual magnitude or whole variation magnitude&quot;?</li> </ul>I thought it would be the latter option, but now I am confused. Something like Electrokinesis is just a toolbox where each power is Mag1. And yet, we have something like Brachiation (generalist) 2 - you get both magnitude 1 effects, which should be ok. Yet it feels slightly like cheating ~ we can choose one power at Mag1, and get 2 more from Mag2 without making it a Mag3 variation.<br /> <br /> I started to think that such &quot;conversion&quot; to higher magnitude are finite in Deviant system (but have no proof yet); you convert M1 &amp; M1 to some &quot;generalist&quot; magnitude 2; and only their M2 &quot;upgrades&quot; can be used to upgrade to Magnitude 3. At least I see that pattern time to time.<br /> <br /> <br /> Another situation, wind-shaman: Mag1 enhanced speed 1 or storm-caller 1; Mag2 brachiation 2 / storm-caller 2, then Mag3 choices are telekinesis 3 or SC3; And M4 gets both M3 powers.<ul><li>Will Mag5 be a new Mag5 power, or mag3 (because M4 is made from two Mag3)? Or maybe separate mag4 power?</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-22T10:30:58-07:00","id":1550319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1550318#post1550318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How should I emulate high Magnitude powers by combining 2 or more lower Mag powers?<br /> I know that Mag3 can be made from 3 Mag1 variations, or 2 Mag2. But if I have Mag2 variations which are made from pairs of Mag1 - it makes things confusing.Or maybe it would be better to ask - &quot;should I calculate each individual magnitude or whole variation magnitude&quot;?<br /> I thought it would be the latter option, but now I am confused. Something like Electrokinesis is just a toolbox where each power is Mag1. And yet, we have something like Brachiation (generalist) 2 - you get both magnitude 1 effects, which should be ok. Yet it feels slightly like cheating ~ we can choose one power at Mag1, and get 2 more from Mag2 without making it a Mag3 variation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Brachiation 2 (Generalist) works exactly like taking Electrokinesis 2 and getting two options from the menu; you get the second power in place of upgrading Bounding or Wall Crawling. Brachiation 3 in turn functionally replaces Generalist with the Magnitude 2 versions of both of the Magnitude 1 options; the &quot;emulate two effects from the preceding Magnitude&quot; approach is preserved, while menu-type Variations like Electrokinesis trade for versatility (and, sometimes, synergy between the different effects).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another situation, wind-shaman: Mag1 enhanced speed 1 or storm-caller 1; Mag2 brachiation 2 / storm-caller 2, then Mag3 choices are telekinesis 3 or SC3; And M4 gets both M3 powers.<br /> <br /> Will Mag5 be a new Mag5 power, or mag3 (because M4 is made from two Mag3)? Or maybe separate mag4 power? </div> </div> </div>This doesn't work because the non-Storm-Caller branch is triple-dipping; assuming this is meant to follow the pattern of two parallel tracks that join up at the end, the Magnitude 2 effect is providing a Magnitude 2 and Magnitude 1 effect from two different Variations, and the Magnitude 3 effect is providing a Magnitude 3 effect from a third Variation.<br /> <br /> That said, yes, if you were to continue the structure as a combination of existing Variations you would either make the Magnitude 5 effect by adding a Magnitude 4 effect from a different Variation, bump up one of the component Variations (e.g. increase Storm Caller to 4), or devise a new synergistic effect that builds on the existing parts.<br /> <br /> As Shallow Graves describes it, creating a new Variation by combining parts of existing Variations can be approached as though you were entangling multiple Tiered Variations with the same Scar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-08T14:25:30-07:00","id":1550856,"title":"","content":"I ask for opinions here.<br /> Deviant seems to have a pretty self-centered mood. So do you think it makes sense for a party of Remades to go on quest to save a stranger Remade and risking to blow up their clandestinity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-08T16:07:46-07:00","id":1550865,"title":"","content":"Absolutely. Pretty core story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-08T19:26:50-07:00","id":1550872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1550856#post1550856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ask for opinions here.<br /> Deviant seems to have a pretty self-centered mood. So do you think it makes sense for a party of Remades to go on quest to save a stranger Remade and risking to blow up their clandestinity?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are core Merits for having a Virtue despite the Divergence and for being better at and mechanically rewarded for keeping Baselines from being harmed by the Web of Pain, to say nothing of the Merit that explicitly gives you Beats for saving other deviants who aren't part of your cohort.<br /> <br /> Even setting aside matters of altruism, there is strength in numbers (especially when those numbers have superpowers) and a deviant saved from trouble is generally a deviant out of the hands of your enemy.<br /> <br /> Like, this isn't a matter of opinion, this is an established potential course of events within the text and genre for both emotional and practical reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-14T09:19:54-07:00","id":1551015,"title":"","content":"Thank you, so the Deviant mood can be less selfish than I figured.<br /> <br /> Now, someone can give me a prewiev of the new Forms in Clade Companion, please?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2457,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","user":"Ipergigio","date":". 05-14-2025, 12:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-14T17:16:17-07:00","id":1551029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1551015#post1551015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, someone can give me a prewiev of the new Forms in Clade Companion, please?</div> </div> </div> </div>Automatons are treated, mechanically, as objects, using Structure and Durability instead of Health. Uplifts use the statblock of an animal as the basis for their Physical actions, modified by the Physical Attribute dots they get as a starting character and purchase with Experiences. Both use their unmodified Attributes for relevant Variation calculations, and for obvious reasons the two are the only two mutually exclusive Forms in the book.<br /> <br /> Outsiders are Deviants who weren't human before the Divergence and therefore have some difficulty in handling unfamiliar Social Skills and first impressions before they get some Acclimation, and the Root of whatever they used to be may mean they have non-Divergence-based abilities and difficulties based on that, though powerful abilities tend to mean they destabilize more rapidly than a similar human-based Deviant. (Automatons have a similar challenge from abilities they gain from being a haunted locket or a brain-uploaded computer, though the degree of individual power doesn't factor into it and Acclimation is used to mitigate the greater Instability.)<br /> <br /> Uplifts, Automata, and Outsiders assume at the basic level that the character has all the normal capabilities of a human character unless otherwise noted, with those exceptions being modeled using Natural Variations and Natural Scars, which work as normal Variations and Scars apart from not being considered supernatural effects and therefore not being subject to effects that raise or lower Magnitude and not being capable of engaging a Clash of Wills (though Natural Scars can still entangle Variations and otherwise do not count as unentangled Scars for the purposes of gaining new Scars; Natural Variations come out of your normal starting Magnitude, although you can also spend Merit dots as part of the Form (Scar-free Natural Variations cost double).<br /> <br /> All three of the above also adjust the cost of their Form(s) in Merit dots and Attribute dots based on the Size of their form and/or whether or not their form counts as a swarm (with larger bodies and more damaging swarms costing more), in addition to the ability to have Natural Variations and Scars.<br /> <br /> Disconnected from the above systems on their own (though still compatible with any of the other Forms), the Myriads are functionally immune to death. When they die, they come back to life in a new body through methods set by the subcategory they belong to, which affects some of the things they can spend Merit dots on the Form to benefit from: Serials resurrect in a consistent location at the start of the next chapter, and can spend Merit dots to make this &quot;facility&quot; more portable and/or numerous (or gain a cost break on the Form by making their facility some level of hostile or dangerous to reincarnate in); Projections resurrect within standard Directed long range of the site of their death via the narrative justification of an appropriate Variation that they have and can spend Merit dots to reincarnate faster or not need to have a Variation that explains how they come back from the dead.<br /> <br /> Both categories of Myriad default to starting every story by taking a major Instability, take a medium Instability whenever they die, reincarnate into an identical body, and have to die to change/reset their bodies; by spending Merit dots, they can reduce the degree of the per-story Instability, start an incarnation without their Physical Scars (losing access to their entangled Variations during that time but setting the timeframe in which they come back at character creation), or making their incarnations not identical (this last effect being a scaled effect called Models, with the level of potential change progressing from cosmetic to Physical Attributes to Physical Variations to Physical Scars - an additional effect that requires Models allows the Myriad to abandon their incarnation at will for a lesser Instability cost than dying); they can also get cost breaks by making it so that their incarnations start without any of their Variations until a certain amount of time has passed, making it so that they need outside help to reincarnate, or (if they have Models) leaving the relevant details of their new body up to the Storyteller rather than their player's choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-15T05:58:51-07:00","id":1551038,"title":"","content":"Basically with this expansion you can play as a twi'lek, as a T-800, as a sentient dog or even as a Rei Ayanami?<br /> <br /> It's pretty thrilling!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-18T10:03:58-07:00","id":1551128,"title":"","content":"Can I use offset in one form to benefit another, or is it only mine interpretation?<br /> <br /> I tried to recreate one character as a deviant, but simple task of recreating a low-medium tier &quot;barely-occultist&quot; end up with standing 4-6 conspiracy (surprisingly, could be accurate) and 2-4 forms (interpretations), I've started making a new one just to fix blind spots in the mechanics, which maybe lower form number to 1-2.<br /> I know, there are no sense in one form with negative cost only, yet if we combine it with another - they make some balance (especially with flexibility in Shallow Graves). Good Myriad traits, but oppressive Symbiont.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-18T10:59:50-07:00","id":1551129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1551128#post1551128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I use offset in one form to benefit another, or is it only mine interpretation?<br /> <br /> I tried to recreate one character as a deviant, but simple task of recreating a low-medium tier &quot;barely-occultist&quot; end up with standing 4-6 conspiracy (surprisingly, could be accurate) and 2-4 forms (interpretations), I've started making a new one just to fix blind spots in the mechanics, which maybe lower form number to 1-2.<br /> I know, there are no sense in one form with negative cost only, yet if we combine it with another - they make some balance (especially with flexibility in Shallow Graves). Good Myriad traits, but oppressive Symbiont.</div> </div> </div> </div>Per Shallow Graves, the net cost of a Form cannot be less than 0 Merit dots; per the Clade Companion, a Myriad form with a negative net Merit dot cost does not provide any benefits to the Remade.<br /> <br /> What is the character you're trying to recreate as a deviant and why are you ending up with such high Standing and so many Forms?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-18T16:10:33-07:00","id":1551133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1551129#post1551129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the character you're trying to recreate as a deviant and why are you ending up with such high Standing and so many Forms?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is unpolished mess which originally supposed to be a 5 minute mental exercise. Maybe it is my specific way of making unpolished mess - got random thought to remade some char as a deviant because you are curious, then drop all what you know about them - get variations/scars; and now we can optimize that and lower magnitude. I once made a fantasy overlord in 5 minutes with 10-12 Magnitude total; but cyber-thug from CP2077 can have same among or more.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I think, I found a problematical parts in my method of remaking. If I'll fix that - it will help to lower standing and allows to keep more variations (instead of sacrificing them). What I tried to recreate:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Ambiguous Origin. Character just born that way, <b>Origin: Genotypal;</b> but we have 0 active powers by default, and those few gained are mostly result of &quot;devoting&quot; to the specific &quot;lifestyle/aspect&quot;, which makes them look like an accident. Had some thoughts about <u><b>Adopted </b></u>in <b><u>Ambivalent</u></b> Form.</li> <li>Clade Paradox. Character is physically a normal human (small anomalies in biology), capable of perceiving otherworldly intrusion/entities, but without any powers to influence the mind. <b>Coactive + </b><u><b>Cousin </b></u>in <b><u>Transitional </u></b>Form.</li> <li>Forms: Why so many Forms? Interpretations of characters powers/luck/occult shenanigans. Most of them keep their net cost 0 or 2. There are <u><b>two</b></u> Forms which I really need to <i><u>finish character concept</u></i>: <b>Ambivalent </b>and <b>Transitional</b>. I suspect adding Myriad was my hubris which make things harder.</li> <li>Variations: Well, powers manifested similar to <u>Monstrous Transformation</u> and 2 <u>cyclic variations</u>. But, to pay all cost of Myriad (I think it was a mistake) and Transitional Forms - I decided to sell 4-6 variations in ambivalent to get few more points to offset.</li> </ol><ul><li>I predict a question: Why didn't I choose mutant's adaptation (in SG) which can shift scars/variations? I thought I was close to finish a character... I don't like to rework almost things that are literally on the finishing line. And by char concept, it is less a sentient choice, but more like automatic adaptation. Go in the wild and become feral, you slowly become more feral and slowly body adapts.</li> <li>MT is mostly a main reason why I took Admixture to mix coactive and chimeric.</li> <li>My new theoretical form which may fix it - mostly mixed cyclic variations/scars, with additional limits similar to caveat/preparation. But it is in WIP. It should fix my overcomplicated solution.</li> </ul><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1551129#post1551129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Per Shallow Graves, the net cost of a Form cannot be less than 0 Merit dots; per the Clade Companion, a Myriad form with a negative net Merit dot cost does not provide any benefits to the Remade.</div> </div> </div> </div><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>If we can combine their total cost/offset it will make more sense.</li> <li>It can be part of the character backstory - escaped conspiracy#1, but you are just one of 200 clones. Same body, same facility.</li> <li>Or we can use Summoner Form with willful summon and relatively good accidental coactive deviant; drop most powers to your demon, keep scar-free one as Otherworldly Connection. Now, you can have a problematical summon. Or symbiont, which is more oppressive and parasitic - no benefits, mostly oppression.</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","user":"Alphari","date":". 05-19-2025, 03:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-19T07:49:30-07:00","id":1551136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1551133#post1551133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ambiguous Origin. Character just born that way, <b>Origin: Genotypal;</b> but we have 0 active powers by default, and those few gained are mostly result of &quot;devoting&quot; to the specific &quot;lifestyle/aspect&quot;, which makes them look like an accident. Had some thoughts about <u><b>Adopted </b></u>in <b><u>Ambivalent</u></b> Form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, this sounds like it's just a regular Pathological, because your character's Origin is to do with their perspective on their transformation at the time of the Divergence; there's a reason Genotypal Remade tend to be the product of conspiracies old enough to have an eye on methods of Divergence that require the length of a human childhood to bear fruit.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Clade Paradox. Character is physically a normal human (small anomalies in biology), capable of perceiving otherworldly intrusion/entities, but without any powers to influence the mind. <b>Coactive + </b><u><b>Cousin </b></u>in <b><u>Transitional </u></b>Form. </div> </div> </div>Mental powers are conventionally a Cephalist focus, but also your Clade is how your powers manifest rather than what they do. If their Variations come from their strange biology they're a Mutant; biology can do strange things in the Chronicles of Darkness.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Variations: Well, powers manifested similar to <u>Monstrous Transformation</u> and 2 <u>cyclic variations</u>. But, to pay all cost of Myriad (I think it was a mistake) and Transitional Forms - I decided to sell 4-6 variations in ambivalent to get few more points to offset. </div> </div> </div>For clarity: the mechanical function of Monstrous Transformation is &quot;activate several Variations at the same time as a higher-level Overt Variation.&quot; Does the package of powers in question work that way, or do they just have a bunch of Reflexive Variations that they tend to use at the same time?<br /> <br /> Also, I should add that Cyclic Variation is a Tiered-Only Deviation and MT is a Discrete Variation that does not have the &quot;although Discrete, this Variation can be subject to effects that raise or lower its Magnitude&quot; rider.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> MT is mostly a main reason why I took Admixture to mix coactive and chimeric. </div> </div> </div>You can have MT without being a Chimeric, it just needs to have less than half of your total Variation Magnitude. Is this character &quot;barely an occultist&quot; or are they sporting a bunch of different packages of powers? The latter is a high-Standing target because having a bunch of different powers (and especially having powers it's impossible to have at Magnitude 1) involves a lot of supernatural power just like playing a mage with a bunch of rotes and praxes costs a lot of Experiences even if the character is Gnosis 1. As-written, the only Form from Shallow Graves that can have a negative Merit cost is Dedicated, using the Limited effect to gain up to 10 extra Merit dots.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It can be part of the character backstory - escaped conspiracy#1, but you are just one of 200 clones. Same body, same facility. </div> </div> </div>Unless the character is coming back to life in a fashion that preserves their current Instabilities, Willpower total, and recent memories, being one of a number of identical clones does not make them a Myriad even if they have Amnesia 5 or a bizarrely frequent Tabula Rasa-based Short Circuit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or we can use Summoner Form with willful summon and relatively good accidental coactive deviant; drop most powers to your demon, keep scar-free one as Otherworldly Connection. Now, you can have a problematical summon. Or symbiont, which is more oppressive and parasitic - no benefits, mostly oppression. </div> </div> </div>A Summoner with Willful still has to summon the homunculus for the effect, and unless positive-cost effects are invested into the Form it vanishes whenever it would take any damage and only has whatever Variations you've assigned to it from your own total. You could have a Durable and Ever-Present Willful homunculus attached to an Involuntary Scar, but the need to have a net total no lower than 0 Merit dots basically anything that would make a Willful homunculus more of a problem to deal with also makes it more than an exercise in how badly you can screw up the character in an un-fun way.<br /> <br /> Similarly, the way the Advanced Symbiote Form works is just that no matter how many different penalty effects it can apply, penalty effects apply no more often than once per scene, the only way a penalty effect applies for longer than a scene is if the character did or failed to do something that would prevent the entity's long-term Aspiration from being resolved, and the positive-cost effects available from Advanced Symbiote include &quot;instead of taking the penalty on the roll itself, you can choose to take Instability or a Condition that allows the ST to cash out the penalty on a later roll.&quot;<br /> <br /> In the interest of not cluttering the Simple Question thread too much, would you like to make a separate thread for sorting out this character?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-19T09:54:24-07:00","id":1551140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1551136#post1551136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">character's Origin is to do with their perspective on their transformation at the time of the Divergence</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, so Genotypal is one who lived with active power from the beginning / childhood... Well, I cut my ambivalent to that origin anyway.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1551136#post1551136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mental powers are conventionally a Cephalist focus</div> </div> </div> </div>The trick is more in the nature of their powers. They focus perception of the world to see more otherworldly stuff; and the rest is mostly touching occult stuff of channeling such power.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1551136#post1551136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the package of powers in question work that way + Cyclic Variation is a Tiered-Only Deviation</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I get it. Maybe relentless will work better.<br /> Agree, I forgot MT is not Tiered. I was more focused on cyclic deviation which rotates Variations. Another good reason to rework character and finish that Form.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1551136#post1551136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can have MT without being a Chimeric</div> </div> </div> </div>I used it to pack few magnitude into one variation - you know, poor decisions and sacrificed variations...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1551136#post1551136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this character &quot;barely an occultist&quot; or are they sporting a bunch of different packages of powers?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think barely. It looks like this: One group has flight 2 and hyper-competence (I'm still thinking what will fit as &quot;aura&quot; of authority) and dependent variation Lash 2 (which target very specific things).<br /> Another one is mostly the same, Hyper-Competence 2, some could have HC 3 [skills slightly vary] (i thought about limiting hc to just few specific directions/specs), Specialized Senses (animal) [different animals], one specific form has Flight 3 (the whole idea of that specific transformation). idk HC or Lash 1 for biting (just stronger bite).<br /> on the other hand Body Modification has most of that, I thought about combining it with caveat (if it works that way).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1551136#post1551136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the interest of not cluttering the Simple Question thread too much, would you like to make a separate thread for sorting out this character?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yesterday I did some revision of the whole sheet &amp; concept. Cutting myriad &amp; unfunny summon helped with magnitude deficit; I now have only Transitional (cost 2).<br /> I think I could finish it without much of a problem.<br /> Thanks for help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-08T12:55:42-08:00","id":1558189,"title":"","content":"From Shallow Graves:<br /> <br /> If you're a Summoner whose Homunculus Scar is Asset (p119), does every person who benefits from the Scar get a separate instance of the deviant's Homunculus?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-12T08:01:28-07:00","id":1559372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1558189#post1558189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From Shallow Graves:<br /> <br /> If you're a Summoner whose Homunculus Scar is Asset (p119), does every person who benefits from the Scar get a separate instance of the deviant's Homunculus?</div> </div> </div> </div>Late to the party, but I believe Homunculus is bound to the Scar. By pure mechanic, raw, Asset gives variations. Homuncul is not a variation.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Transmissible form bounded to Asset or your Homuncul or rite of summoning \u2248 now influence of your homuncul or Asset gifted variations may transform baseline into Deviant (Dedicated / Latent or Temporary (Transmissible form) &amp; Transitional with Summoner form).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-12T08:36:29-07:00","id":1559373,"title":"","content":"<br /> If deviant found/made a localised timeloop - How to write it in CC Realm mechanics?<br /> Loop resets everything (including deviants, at least physically, maybe) but technically only few individuals will remember loops. And each loop is like a transferring few chosen ones to the beginning.<br /> There is no physical area where people needs to be to transfer back, people are not locked in a timeloop while world around moving on.<br /> <br /> So is it even a Realm? There is an example in CC (Alternate Time) - cultists hunt someone, and he relives each loop as a nightmare. While everything is fine, I just don't know how to describe it as a Realm.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-12T09:03:15-07:00","id":1559375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1559373#post1559373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If deviant found/made a localised timeloop - How to write it in CC Realm mechanics?<br /> Loop resets everything (including deviants, at least physically, maybe) but technically only few individuals will remember loops. And each loop is like a transferring few chosen ones to the beginning.<br /> There is no physical area where people needs to be to transfer back, people are not locked in a timeloop while world around moving on.<br /> <br /> So is it even a Realm? There is an example in CC (Alternate Time) - cultists hunt someone, and he relives each loop as a nightmare. While everything is fine, I just don't know how to describe it as a Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming I've parsed the explanation correctly, the Spatial Extent is at least World, the Temporal Extent is Loop, and the Accessibility sounds Key-based, with the Key being whatever determines which characters enter (and leave) the loop.<br /> <br /> If it's not meaningfully different from the setting the characters are in before they enter the loop then the distinction between Realm and isolated incident is kind of academic, so knowing the age and internal duration of the loop is kind of the deciding factor \u2014 it's one thing if we're talking about a year-long loop that's been running since a hundred years ago and another if everyone's been reliving the same week for a month or so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-24T21:34:27-07:00","id":1559612,"title":"","content":"Does the insulating effect of Catharsis against automatic minor Instabilities at the start of the story apply to any other sources of start-of-story Instability, such as the Clean Adaptation, the Unstable effect of the Ambivalent or Transitional Forms, the tradeoff of having certain amounts or levels of Natural Variations as an Automaton or Outsider, or the penultimate level of the Stable effect of being a Myriad, or does that only apply to the [highest Variation Magnitude] minor Instabilities from the core rules?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-22T05:33:06-07:00","id":1560149,"title":"","content":"I'm still looking for a way how to shape a Sin-eater-like Deviant using the core rules only.<br /> <br /> A deviace that inflicts an anchor-like condition to the character and allows the spirit to manifest itself into the material world?<br /> <br /> Maybe a build with symbiote form to mimic the anchor condition, and a set of variations to emulate manifestations and numina can work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2457,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","user":"Ipergigio","date":". 05-22-2026, 08:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-22T06:59:55-07:00","id":1560151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1560149#post1560149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still looking for a way how to shape a Sin-eater-like Deviant using the core rules only.<br /> <br /> A deviace that inflicts an anchor-like condition to the character and allows the spirit to manifest itself into the material world?<br /> <br /> Maybe a build with symbiote form to mimic the anchor condition, and a set of variations to emulate manifestations and numina can work?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are only using the core rules, anything that specifically relies on the ephemeral being mechanics is beyond consideration.<br /> <br /> The Clades Companion says that Otherworldly Connection 5 will allow you to manifest ephemeral beings (typically emulating Image or Materialize, though if they know other common Manifestations they might be compelled to use those), but below that level you're looking at either a unique plot device or something outside the character's control a la the Monstrous subtype of the Conspicuous Appearance Scar.<br /> <br /> It's very important not to confuse the metaphysical explanation for the character's powers with their mechanical effect. Since you've brought this up a couple of times with long gaps between, it may be worth either clarifying what you actually want the thing to do or making a separate thread to do so, because wholesale build advice is kind of out-of-scope with a thread for simple questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-22T10:17:51-07:00","id":1560152,"title":"","content":"My bad... I failed to find my old post and so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-23T09:20:00-07:00","id":1560164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1560152#post1560152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My bad... I failed to find my old post and so...</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1481773-deviant-symbiote-and-alternate-persona\">This one</a>? Or your posts from earlier in this thread <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1482378#post1482378\">here</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1478958-deviant-ask-a-simple-question-renegade-style?p=1497559#post1497559\">here</a>?<br /> <br /> Either way, the specific limitation of using only the corebook means we're going to need more information than is practical for this thread to determine how to meet your goal.<br /> <br /> Without the ability to use Advanced Forms, the ephemeral being mechanics, or the Cyclical Variation/Scar Deviations from other books, anything you want to accomplish is going to need to be modeled with corebook Variations and Scars, which will require defining what abilities and problems the character's occult state gives them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}